  str_mission_name_4220100 = "Heresy",
  str_mission_name_4220110 = "Arcana",
  str_mission_name_4220125 = "Eeriness",
  str_mission_desc_4001010 = "For the first time in 17 years, you tried your psychic ability. Was this young lady before you a chance for you to leave this place?",
  str_mission_desc_4001020 = "You had never seen your people before but now you have a friend.",
  str_mission_desc_4001030 = "Perhaps the Colossus was ready to be activated?",
  str_mission_desc_4001040 = "The Aurorians would not stop fighting as long as there was light.",
  str_mission_desc_4001041 = "There were more and more Eclipsites. You'd better try other ways if things were getting tougher.",
  str_mission_desc_4001042 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001043 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001044 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001045 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001046 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001047 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4001050 = "Guided by Ms. Blanc, you have a clearer idea of how to get to the destination.",
  str_mission_desc_4001051 = "You fought easier in battles than before. The Aurorians and you matched up quite well now.",
  str_mission_desc_4001060 = "Your battles got tougher, witnessing growth of the Aurorians and you.",
  str_mission_desc_4001070 = "At the critical moment, the ground started to shake and something was approaching...",
  str_mission_desc_4001080 = "Soroz couldn't take off for now. Before it could work, you had to fight against countless Eclipsites.",
  str_mission_desc_4001090 = "The Eclipsites had been found in every area on the Colossus. Defend to the end!",
  str_mission_desc_4001100 = "An increasing number of the Eclipsites invaded the vital section on the Colossus - the Bridge.",
  str_mission_desc_4001101 = "Some unknown crises lurked around you.",
  str_mission_desc_4001110 = "If you can't win by numbers, schemes are the way to go.",
  str_mission_desc_4001120 = "You must leave with all your companions!",
  str_mission_desc_4001130 = "Accompanied by the engine's roar, the Colossus blasted off. However, a rival who was stronger than Kraken walked out of the shadow.",
  str_mission_desc_4002015 = "An ally's sacrifice and the unexpected news... All of this seemed to cast a shadow over the path forward. Where will everything go from here?",
  str_mission_desc_4002010 = "Soroz crashed in the wilderness due to malfunction.",
  str_mission_desc_4002035 = "Test",
  str_mission_desc_4002020 = "You'd be commanding a group of bumbling guys this time...",
  str_mission_desc_4002030 = "The Rediesel Wrench was strong beyond all doubt. However, the Eclipsites in force brought you into a stalemate.",
  str_mission_desc_4002031 = "Hold on! Illumina's reinforcements might be on the way. You got to tough it out.",
  str_mission_desc_4002040 = "Considering combat possibilities and Vice's injury, the aggressive Rediesel Wrench guys forced you into a corner.",
  str_mission_desc_4002050 = "The situation isn't looking too good. The Eclipsites seem to be charging towards the Colossus...",
  str_mission_desc_4002060 = "While everyone was guessing if a high-level Eclipsite was in charge, a new Eclipsite, Umbrahulk, appeared.",
  str_mission_desc_4002070 = "Commanded by Nozard, the Eclipsites had threatened the citizens in the undercity. To conserve your strength, you had no choice but to retreat!",
  str_mission_desc_4002080 = "You were attacked unprepared by the Eclipsites. But fortunately, it was not too late...",
  str_mission_desc_4002090 = "The undercity was captured by the Eclipsites. Was it the end?",
  str_mission_desc_4002100 = "Undercity 28 had fallen, and in Charon's hand was the final means to end the enemies with everyone altogether.",
  str_mission_desc_4002101 = "Let the injured and citizens embark on the Colossus! It was not the time to relax yet!",
  str_mission_desc_4002110 = "The increasing weight of responsibility fell on you. Friends, superiors, and citizens... What course to follow...?",
  str_mission_desc_4002120 = [[
When surrounded, Charon cried out deafeningly to urge you 
to leave. He would fall with Undercity 28...]],
  str_mission_desc_4003010 = "With the help of Vice and Soroz, seeking your people seemed to go well.",
  str_mission_desc_4003020 = "One of your people asked you for help. He appeared to have run into danger?!",
  str_mission_desc_4003030 = "Seems like you were beaten to the punch. There are traces of Eclipsites everywhere.",
  str_mission_desc_4003031 = "The signal isn't good. \"That Person\" is being chased. You gotta hurry up.",
  str_mission_desc_4003040 = "The path leading to the relics was rough and uphill, hogged by the Eclipsites.",
  str_mission_desc_4003050 = "A mass of Eclipsites poured in. Who was behind all these?",
  str_mission_desc_4003060 = "You found him! But he was being hunted down by \nenemies who turned traitors —",
  str_mission_desc_4003070 = "No one could tell how strong your enemies were. Even so... There was no way back.",
  str_mission_desc_4003080 = "Schummer got her hands on the Think Tank Module. It was too late—But you shall not escape!",
  str_mission_desc_4003090 = "Mendelson was getting weaker and weaker, but you kept moving forward without hesitation.",
  str_mission_desc_4003091 = "You were getting closer to the destination. Did you smell your enemies?",
  str_mission_desc_4003100 = "The air was full of uncertainties, covered with a heavy mist sprawling into the dark.",
  str_mission_desc_4003110 = "The dark energy was dominating Mendelson inch by inch physically. His body was like a candle in the wind!",
  str_mission_desc_4003120 = "Surrounded by darkness and unrest, you heard a faint rustle of communication among high-level Eclipsites. The ultimate trial was ahead.",
  str_mission_desc_4004010 = "The east area of Lower Lumopolis was invaded by the Eclipsites. Time is of the essence and you must win this.",
  str_mission_desc_4004020 = "The Eclipsites were spotted in the west area! The runaway ones raised the devil everywhere.",
  str_mission_desc_4004030 = [[
The number of Eclipsites was more than you thought. Evacuation and asylum were before everything 
for the townsfolk.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004031 = [[
Guardians were wiping out the remnants of the Eclipsites one by one. None of them could 
escape their hunt.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004040 = [[
At a remote corner of the west area, the Eclipsites summoned had been waiting 
for a long time.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004050 = "The Eclipsites attacked over and over again, which could be just a cover-up...",
  str_mission_desc_4004060 = "Shelt decided to do whatever it takes for her own ends: She awakened her sister, who had also turned into an Eclipsite...",
  str_mission_desc_4004070 = "Focus on tracking down the Eclipsite sisters and take down reckless pests.",
  str_mission_desc_4004080 = "The Eclipsite sisters did not do it on the spur of the moment, summoning the Eclipsites in an endless stream.",
  str_mission_desc_4004090 = "It was getting closer. You almost caught the ringleader who planned these disturbances.",
  str_mission_desc_4004091 = "Kill them all. None shall be spared.",
  str_mission_desc_4004100 = "Where was the suspicious man? Who the hell was he?",
  str_mission_desc_4004110 = "The Eclipsite sisters' blood tarnished this city. They had no way back.",
  str_mission_desc_4004120 = "It was time to put the sisters on trial. How would the despairing enemies resist...",
  str_mission_desc_4005010 = "The number of fallen Colossi indicated the number of sacrificed Caelestites, as well as the number of Eclipsites with blood on their hands...",
  str_mission_desc_4005020 = "The interior of the fallen Colossus was badly damaged, so the path leading to the Autonomous Growth Unit was bumpy and turbulent.",
  str_mission_desc_4005030 = "Danger lurked among the relics, as the Eclipsites suddenly appeared from the shadows.",
  str_mission_desc_4005031 = "Hitting the Achilles' heel was the key to get out of danger.",
  str_mission_desc_4005040 = "Be on the alert. You might get hurt because by the Eclipsites, as well as unnoticed traps.",
  str_mission_desc_4005050 = "Good bait can escape unscathed with its moves.",
  str_mission_desc_4005060 = "A pious melody was played gently. The Colossus started glowing again from its dormancy. This was the last gift, my people.",
  str_mission_desc_4005070 = "The chance comer on the Colossus messed your thoughts. Solutions needed to be thought out at length.",
  str_mission_desc_4005080 = "Pursuing soldiers were overflowing like annoying flies as time passed.",
  str_mission_desc_4005090 = "Just 5 minutes left before the deadline. What was your decision?",
  str_mission_desc_4005091 = "Careful evasion and bold strategies were indispensable.",
  str_mission_desc_4005100 = "Be proactive, and don't be a sitting duck.",
  str_mission_desc_4005110 = "There was always a way and you'd see it if you'd adapt.",
  str_mission_desc_4005120 = "The countdown was going to be over. Would a surprise attack turn the tide? It was time to deal a deathblow to Schummer!",
  str_mission_desc_4006010 = "When chasing after the Flame Control Module in Whispering Corridor, you found army boots' prints. It must belong to the traitor, Gertzurde.",
  str_mission_desc_4006020 = "To be ahead of Schummer, you hastened your search.",
  str_mission_desc_4006030 = "One enemy ambush followed another as Carleen and Vice strove to find the Flame Control Module as quickly as possible...",
  str_mission_desc_4006031 = "Darkness, coldness, and stillness...Fighting alone was unbearable, but were you really without support?",
  str_mission_desc_4006040 = "Even with Ms. Sheol's remote support, the devious windings in Whispering Corridor plunged you into confusion.",
  str_mission_desc_4006050 = "Gertzurde seemed to be lurking ahead. Would this be the final battle?",
  str_mission_desc_4006060 = "\"You... killed Shelt!\" The avenger had shown up in before you...",
  str_mission_desc_4006070 = "The Flame Control Module was near at hand. What was the enemy up to...",
  str_mission_desc_4006080 = "The number of Eclipsites was increasing, and the constant battling had everyone exhausted...",
  str_mission_desc_4006090 = "Never rest... Gertzurde's footsteps were approaching and you could sense the familiar scent of revenge.",
  str_mission_desc_4006091 = "Whatever impasses you faced, your companions would come for you regardless of the dangers...",
  str_mission_desc_4006100 = "You were not stopped by the traps and ambushers along the way. There was a question Gertzurde must ask Schummer...",
  str_mission_desc_4006110 = "At last, you have reached the depths of the Whispering Corridor, and if nothing \"unexpected\" happens, the Flame Control Module should be here...",
  str_mission_desc_4006120 = "Would Gertzurde get what he wanted? Would Schummer fulfill his death-match manifesto? Your journey had nearly come to an end.",
  str_mission_desc_4007010 = "You decided to split up to ensure that support and rescue operations were carried out at the same time.",
  str_mission_desc_4007020 = "Numerous Eclipsites flooded Lower Lumopolis, but your operations seemed to be going well?",
  str_mission_desc_4007030 = "You felt distraught at the fact that you could not sense Soroz, but you had to protect the townsfolk of Lower Lumopolis, even if you were without combat ability...",
  str_mission_desc_4007031 = "At this moment, something was brewing in Lumopolis...",
  str_mission_desc_4007040 = [[
In the teeth of threat over your head and wild street battles, this was a trial
 you've never experienced.]],
  str_mission_desc_4007050 = "Support operations in Lower Lumopolis were done, but the Uptown was being attacked?!",
  str_mission_desc_4007060 = "As you were heading to Uptown, a familiar but strange enemy appeared, huge and scary...",
  str_mission_desc_4007070 = "This was a battle for what everyone wanted to protect—",
  str_mission_desc_4007080 = "The battle was a live-or-die game that you had to race against time to win.",
  str_mission_desc_4007090 = "Panic gradually built up without cease. You cannot let these Eclipsites wreck Soroz again!",
  str_mission_desc_4007100 = "A message from Soroz. Could it be...?!",
  str_mission_desc_4007110 = "The temperature around started to quickly plunge and you could smell Schummer, there!",
  str_mission_desc_4007111 = "Was Soroz's 'self-awareness' component really gone? Would your bond with it vanish?",
  str_mission_desc_4007120 = [[
Schummer became a totally different person after possessing all the modules.
Was this a battle or just a unilateral... game?]],
  str_mission_desc_4008020 = "Schummer was holding you within Aviduz, so Vice came to save you. You decided to find Chief Vivian and take her with you...",
  str_mission_desc_4008030 = "As you moved onward, your body felt strange, but there was no time for you to check what's wrong. You had to find Vivian as soon as possible.",
  str_mission_desc_4008040 = "You trod on lightly and quickly dealt with the enemies in your path.",
  str_mission_desc_4008041 = "Misled, switching sides, and backstabbing... The Eclipsites will be caught off guard.",
  str_mission_desc_4008050 = "The interior of the Black Colossus was complexly laid out, so you had to be very careful...",
  str_mission_desc_4008060 = "Schummer hasn't found you yet. Keep going—maybe Chief Vivian is in the room ahead!",
  str_mission_desc_4008070 = "As Curies barged her way through, you finally reached where Chief Vivian was being held, and where a powerful enemy awaited you...",
  str_mission_desc_4008090 = "Chief Vivian had been successfully rescued, so the most urgent task then was to leave this ominous place. But was this really the most rational choice?",
  str_mission_desc_4008100 = "A loud noise sounded. The situation had changed. Was Carleen successful, or had Schummer finally triumphed!?",
  str_mission_desc_4008110 = "Your strategy had changed from escape to attack! This was your last chance to cripple the enemy from within!",
  str_mission_desc_4008111 = "What trials and tribulations can you expect from the ominous Aviduz?",
  str_mission_desc_4008120 = "The path leading to the bridge was filled with danger, and the Eclipsites descended in a frenzy...",
  str_mission_desc_4008130 = "Keep moving—Schummer should be close by!",
  str_mission_desc_4008140 = "Finally, the decisive moment came. Lumopolis and the Black Colossus—today, one would fall, and you shall bear witness to it all...",
  str_mission_desc_4009020 = "You followed Aviduz's trail of debris and found yourself back in Eraveil, where everything began.",
  str_mission_desc_4009030 = "Could there be someone else here besides the Eclipsites?",
  str_mission_desc_4009040 = "Even more danger lied ahead, as well as a certain familiar face...",
  str_mission_desc_4009041 = "Find their weaknesses and use the enemy to defeat the enemy.",
  str_mission_desc_4009050 = "With Sinsa joining the party, exploring Eraveil became a much easier task.",
  str_mission_desc_4009060 = "The abundance of Darkflow may have turned the air cold, but you must move on.",
  str_mission_desc_4009070 = "Strong emotions cut through the air. Where did that cry come from? Was it an Eclipsite?",
  str_mission_desc_4009090 = "The ground shook and a fearsome aura surged forth...",
  str_mission_desc_4009100 = "Use your psychic abilities to push forward and find a way to break through the enemy's formation!",
  str_mission_desc_4009110 = "It's like the enemies were coming out of the walls, and they even seemed to be operating in unison.",
  str_mission_desc_4009111 = "If you can't defeat the enemy head-on, try creating an opportunity from another angle.",
  str_mission_desc_4009120 = "A difficult enemy appeared... It's time to rid Eraveil of their evil presence!",
  str_mission_desc_4009130 = "An even stronger enemy lied in wait. Before facing the battle ahead, you must escape the Eclipsite siege...",
  str_mission_desc_4009140 = "The wreckage of Aviduz lied ahead! But who was that standing in front of it!?",
  str_mission_desc_4010020 = "Aviduz was right in front of you. Pursuing Forsakin, confirming whether Schummer is still alive... whatever happened next, your only option was to enter...",
  str_mission_desc_4010030 = "Through your psychic abilities, you deduced that Schummer had been... eating Eclipsites!?",
  str_mission_desc_4010040 = "Not all of the Eclipsites were running for their lives—some of them were prepared to fight you to the death.",
  str_mission_desc_4010041 = "If the odds are ever stacked against you, try to make use of your environment to shift the advantage in your favor!",
  str_mission_desc_4010050 = "Countless Eclipsites roamed within Aviduz, like aimless maggots within a festering corpse.",
  str_mission_desc_4010060 = "The Eclipsites appeared to be hell-bent on blocking your way forward.",
  str_mission_desc_4010070 = "Another familiar enemy appeared. It appeared Forsakin's resurrection magic could not be underestimated...",
  str_mission_desc_4010090 = "Upon confirming your dream about Eraveil, your anger was ignited once again.",
  str_mission_desc_4010100 = "The enemy standing before you seemed to possess the ability to seal Luminatics! This was going to be a tough battle.",
  str_mission_desc_4010110 = "The Eclipsites blocking the path had no intention of giving up without a fight.",
  str_mission_desc_4010111 = "It seemed like there's no end to this constant stream of Eclipsites...",
  str_mission_desc_4010120 = "The Eclipsites were trying to force you into a hopeless situation!",
  str_mission_desc_4010130 = "Schummer was just up ahead. You didn't need to use your psychic abilities to know this—the trembling ground and rampant Darkflow were indications enough.",
  str_mission_desc_4010140 = "Defeat Schummer!",
  str_mission_desc_4101020 = "Oppressed by the Darkflow, you face more difficulties in battle. But you can't shrink back for the safety of Soroz!",
  str_mission_desc_4101030 = "In the depths of the Undercity, traces of war are buried along with other secrets...",
  str_mission_desc_4101040 = "How did High-Level Eclipsites get here? Run! Don't stop!",
  str_mission_desc_4101060 = "Reinhardt has been watching you. To ensure your safety, she's been consumed by anxiety and worries.",
  str_mission_desc_4101070 = "What on earth happened in Undercity 80? Maybe Reinhardt has an answer.",
  str_mission_desc_4101080 = "Soon you will land. Would there be hope for a safe return awaiting?",
  str_mission_desc_4101090 = "Long-lasting hatred can't be easily soothed. Sometimes, leaving might be the best choice.",
  str_mission_desc_4201020 = "Soroz is being ambushed by Eclipsites? Let's not panic. We'll get them off the Colossus!",
  str_mission_desc_4201030 = "The fact that Eclipsites managed to attack Soroz indicates that someone's behind all this. This was no simple ambush!",
  str_mission_desc_4201040 = "Anyhow, it's not a crash if it lands where it's supposed to.",
  str_mission_desc_4201041 = "Encountering Eclipsites while searching for the entrance wasn't part of the plan, but no time to waste, let's take them out quickly.",
  str_mission_desc_4201050 = "It's a good thing you've got a metal detector to help kickstart our search for the entrance. But, can it really find something useful?",
  str_mission_desc_4201060 = "This place is empty... All that's left are echoes and fragments of the past.",
  str_mission_desc_4201061 = "Continue exploring and searching... Let's do our best to find the light of hope in the depths.",
  str_mission_desc_4201070 = "An unknown presence watches the battle, and it's following your every move.",
  str_mission_desc_4201080 = "Don't stop and don't look back. Keep running onwards and seeking that silver lining.",
  str_mission_desc_4201090 = "What wicked acts must one commit to be exiled to such an abyss?",
  str_mission_desc_4201100 = "It's not here, but deeper. Keep moving forward, but stay wary of threats from the past.",
  str_mission_desc_4201120 = "Caelestites, Aurorians, Eclipsites, Colossi... Wonder how many secrets lie hidden in this vast, long-abandoned base...",
  str_mission_desc_4201130 = "It isn't just the walls and gates of the base that guard these secrets, but those Eclipsites here as well.",
  str_mission_desc_4201140 = "The Neural Aux is damaged, and there's no way to input commands correctly. How about... rebooting it first?",
  str_mission_desc_4202020 = "There seem to be Eclipsites in this tower. Were they already here to begin with?",
  str_mission_desc_4202030 = "As you continue moving on, you encounter something unknown and unexpected.",
  str_mission_desc_4202040 = "You've been hearing strange noises behind you for a while now. Are Eclipsites on your trail... or something else?",
  str_mission_desc_4202041 = "Since when have Eclipsites gotten smart enough to use traps?! Keep your eyes open, and let's defeat them!",
  str_mission_desc_4202050 = "What's with all these traps leading to the Chord Zone?! Wonder if they could be put to use...",
  str_mission_desc_4202060 = "Barton decided to use the Chord Link in order to escape this difficult situation. Do what you can to buy him some time!",
  str_mission_desc_4202070 = "Steady there... Just a little longer and things will turn in your favor.",
  str_mission_desc_4202090 = "The battle is raging outside the tower, and reinforcements have finally arrived. Now all that's left is to fight.",
  str_mission_desc_4202100 = "Everyone's giving it their all on the battlefield, but how long can they hold out?",
  str_mission_desc_4202115 = "Aurorians outside the Obelisk of Return are doing their best to find a chance to turn the tide.",
  str_mission_desc_4202111 = "Looks like a troublemaker has entered the battlefield. Time's running out. Let's strike, now!",
  str_mission_desc_4202120 = "There are still Eclipsites blocking the path to the Core Ring and even tougher challenges up ahead.",
  str_mission_desc_4202130 = "There are some things only you can do. Everyone is here, ready to help, so just go for it.",
  str_mission_desc_4202140 = "It's a call to return, not just for you, but for hope.",
  str_mission_desc_4203020 = "In order to better understand Vice's condition, you agree to allow Illumina to research new data modules found on Soroz.",
  str_mission_desc_4203030 = "After entering the simulated battlefield, you begin performing tests according to the researchers' instructions. At the very least, the battles are fairly easy... for now.",
  str_mission_desc_4203040 = "You use the battle simulator once again, but this time the terrain and environment have changed.",
  str_mission_desc_4203041 = "There's chaos and danger all around, and you're completely lost... You can't afford to stay here much longer!",
  str_mission_desc_4203050 = "Hang on. No one said the simulation was going to be this hard!",
  str_mission_desc_4203060 = "What is this place? Why haven't I seen it before? Vice? Reinhardt? Can you guys hear me?",
  str_mission_desc_4203070 = "Desperate soldiers being crushed under a savage Eclipsite onslaught... Is this the end of the world?",
  str_mission_desc_4203090 = "Guardian One, responsible for the entirety of the Illumina Federation's daily operations... looks smaller than expected.",
  str_mission_desc_4203100 = "Despite this being your first time meeting Guardian One, a pure and natural sense of trust is established between the two of you.",
  str_mission_desc_4203110 = "It's impossible to stand with both feet on solid ground in a virtual environment. Even so, your only choice is to keep marching forward.",
  str_mission_desc_4203111 = "This experiment seeks to test the limits of one's strength in order to discover even the slightest chance of breaking them.",
  str_mission_desc_4203120 = "Reach out your hand, run faster—you are only a step away from reaching it.",
  str_mission_desc_4203130 = "It's time to fix things. After all, that is why you came here in the first place.",
  str_mission_desc_4203140 = "After an indeterminate amount of time, you eventually arrive at the final glitch.",
  str_mission_desc_4204020 = "The powerful, important weapon known as the \"Combat Cyborg\" is actually...",
  str_mission_desc_4204030 = "Sean returns from the war zone as fast as he can. He received word from the Illumina garrison that you were on the way.",
  str_mission_desc_4204031 = "Sometimes, charging straight into combat is not the best option.",
  str_mission_desc_4204040 = "You continue your journey to Twilight, where three old friends are finally reunited.",
  str_mission_desc_4204050 = "After finally reaching the outskirts of Twilight, the aurora overhead begins to surge out of control, spelling disaster for the those living beneath.",
  str_mission_desc_4204060 = "There are still civilians behind you trying to escape! Do not let even a single Eclipsite get past you!",
  str_mission_desc_4204070 = "A ray of light suddenly illuminates the battlefield, allowing you and your allies to fight without constraints.",
  str_mission_desc_4204090 = "You and your allies are finally ready. The darkness will no longer impede your sight.",
  str_mission_desc_4204100 = "What you've been searching for... Where could it be?",
  str_mission_desc_4204101 = "Find the weak point, aim well, and concentrate your attacks!",
  str_mission_desc_4204115 = "Who is more powerful: Axelia or Sean?",
  str_mission_desc_4204120 = "After no small amount of hardship, you finally find the Colossus that crash-landed in ruins. Victory is just within reach.",
  str_mission_desc_4204130 = "Immediately after copying its data, the Colossus begins to stir. Could another catastrophe be at hand?",
  str_mission_desc_4204140 = "A final poem, offered in your name... A final farewell.",
  str_mission_desc_4205020 = "You are forced by Forsakin to fight Illumina soldiers.",
  str_mission_desc_4205030 = "You once again encounter sentries at the lab entrance.",
  str_mission_desc_4205040 = "You and Vice aren't going to twiddle your thumbs while the experiment goes on. Wait for the right time to reverse the predicament...",
  str_mission_desc_4205041 = "Seize the opportunity to defeat the enemy and escape!",
  str_mission_desc_4205050 = "Your resistance has been Eclipsites summoned by Forsakin in a fiery duel to the death!",
  str_mission_desc_4205070 = "Separated from Vice, your lone self has no choice but to obey Forsakin. You need to follow her will and venture deep into the Undercity.",
  str_mission_desc_4205080 = "To locate both you and Vice, who has long been missing, Carleen follows Gronru's tips to the Undercity.",
  str_mission_desc_4205090 = "Still seeking the files, Forsakin didn't expect keen defenses in the File Archive.",
  str_mission_desc_4205100 = "Tasked with an important mission, Yingel's finally found Vice's whereabouts, only to run into a formidable enemy before the rescue...",
  str_mission_desc_4205101 = "Some enemies will engage you in a long, deadly fight, so be cautious...",
  str_mission_desc_4205110 = "Yingel is fighting a tough battle, while Carleen has made it to Forsakin and will try to get you out of here.",
  str_mission_desc_4205120 = "Forsakin is thrown off-balance by the surprise blaze. Take the opportunity to defeat her and Helios!",
  str_mission_desc_4205130 = "Just when you're about to defeat Forsakin, she thwarts that by cutting off the power to the main gate...",
  str_mission_desc_4205140 = "Forsakin has completed the final upgrade to Helios. It's going to be a brutal fight.",
  str_mission_desc_4206020 = "The first session is virtual fighting through Battle Simulator, and all exercise participants are preparing for it seriously.",
  str_mission_desc_4206030 = "The second session is combat lessons, with a team of training staff led by Wrath passing on brawling know-how to the exercise participants...",
  str_mission_desc_4206040 = "For more course credits, you, Vice, and Carleen decide to apply for additional simulator permits to hone your combat skills.",
  str_mission_desc_4206041 = "The enemies seem to feed off the battle! There has to be a way to end the struggle!",
  str_mission_desc_4206050 = "Before the exercise began, Eclipsites from who-knows-where suddenly emerged in Gannon City. Get rid of them as soon as possible.",
  str_mission_desc_4206060 = "The third session of the Joint Military Exercise is fighting genuine Eclipsites in real combat. Will the participants prevail against so many foes?",
  str_mission_desc_4206070 = "Upon reaching the site for capture-the-flag, the squads split up and go into the Undercity. However, your squad gets into an unexpected fight against Eclipsites.",
  str_mission_desc_4206080 = "The chaotic battle continues and that weird squad proves to be pretty tough...",
  str_mission_desc_4206090 = "You delve farther into the Undercity until haphazardly encountering an even bigger danger in the form of a huge spider-like monstrosity.",
  str_mission_desc_4206110 = "You, Yingel, and others split up to check out Gannon. Sure enough, you run into Eclipsites that slip through the loophole in the defenses!",
  str_mission_desc_4206120 = "The Eclipsite intruders scatter in panic, apparently not intending to fight. You also sense the familiar menace of a certain Wraith...",
  str_mission_desc_4206121 = "Intruders are still present in the city that have to be eliminated as soon as possible.",
  str_mission_desc_4206130 = "Following the Wraith's trails, you come to a certain gate on the lowest level. Figerald is after something in there. Stop him!",
  str_mission_desc_4206140 = "The peons are all out of the way. Now on to Figerald the Wraith!",
  str_mission_desc_4207020 = "You and Vice arrive at the office of Illumina Legion Commanders, hoping for a chance to change the tide. However, before you can even speak, the commanders have already received mission orders and left...",
  str_mission_desc_4207030 = "The citizens of Illumina are buzzing with what's been happening recently. Just as you notice this, an announcement echoes through the Undercity broadcasts, proclaiming the ascension of a new Grand Marshal...",
  str_mission_desc_4207031 = "Eclipsites will soon break out from where they've been confined. Defeat them for the safety of the lab!",
  str_mission_desc_4207040 = "Having just been promoted to Grand Marshal of Illumina, Wrath is already assigned to reinforce the battlefront at Twilight. Yet, as she prepares for departure, she seems to have not felt any of the anticipated joy of becoming the Grand Marshal...",
  str_mission_desc_4207050 = "Reflecting on the past, Wrath has initiated countless challenges against Reinhardt, almost all of which ended in failure, including the final selection for Grand Marshal...",
  str_mission_desc_4207060 = "Joselyne leads the wounded toward safety. However, upon learning of the soldiers' wavering confidence on the battlefield, she contemplates what she can do for them...",
  str_mission_desc_4207080 = "With your psychic abilities, you perceive that the pervasive darkflow in Twilight appears to be maneuvered by a central command. Yet, the main enemy at this center is still shrouded in mystery...",
  str_mission_desc_4207090 = "The arrival of Illumina soldiers momentarily halts the actions of the Eclipsites, yet Forsakin seems to have detected the secret behind these soldiers' enhanced strength...",
  str_mission_desc_4207100 = "As the battle against the Eclipsites rages on, a ripple of abnormal actions spreads among the Illumina soldiers. Speculation grows that the soldiers might be influenced by some enemy acting as the central command...",
  str_mission_desc_4207110 = "Concerned for Axelia on the battlefield, Yingel makes her way to Ulysses' laboratory. Within these walls, she witnesses a cruel experiment...",
  str_mission_desc_4207111 = "The monsters in the quagmires have blocked your way. Defeat them!",
  str_mission_desc_4207120 = "Confronted by the ever-spreading mire and the Eclipsites' assaults, Wrath makes a resolute decision—to plunge into the mud, seeking out the central command enemy hiding in it...",
  str_mission_desc_4207130 = "After clashing with the central command enemy, Wrath's body gradually falls out of her control. Soroz speculates that her consciousness has been swallowed by the mud...",
  str_mission_desc_4207140 = "Axelia's squad has been ensnared in the mud for quite some time. At this moment, Axelia has already lost the ability to assail the Eclipsites, but her lips keep murmuring two special action commands...",
  str_mission_desc_4208020 = "With the mud Eclipsite vanquished, you embark on an all-out search for Wrath's location. However, at this very moment, unexpected changes also begin to manifest among the Illumina soldiers...",
  str_mission_desc_4208030 = "Relief floods over you at Wrath's return, yet her ordeals leave you perplexed. Subsequently, the collective focus shifts toward addressing the wounded soldiers' predicament...",
  str_mission_desc_4208040 = "The tracking squad led by Charon and Vice encounters peculiar resistance, preventing them from reaching the Dark Zone. Meanwhile, aboard the train, a mysterious passenger emerges...",
  str_mission_desc_4208041 = "The condition is getting out of control. The enemies now aim at you; please protect your teammates.",
  str_mission_desc_4208050 = "Victoria has led the group to evade the pursuit of the enigmatic force temporarily. Yet, at this very moment, the Bloody Bible brings forth a new revelation...",
  str_mission_desc_4208060 = "As Wrath searches for her subordinates, a disoriented soldier chokes her on the neck. Everyone is trying to talk sense into her, but she still can't make up her mind...",
  str_mission_desc_4208070 = "Joselyne beseeches Lumo Stronghold to shelter the refugees, only to meet with refusal. But just as the wounded soldiers start to attack the innocent, a powerful voice resounds...",
  str_mission_desc_4208080 = "As the search operation reaches the barriers of Twilight, a staggering sight unfolds before the group's eyes. And the mastermind behind it all, at long last, finally shows up...",
  str_mission_desc_4208100 = "With the mud dissipated, Twilight is left with nothing but shattered walls and ruins. Yet, facing such messy debris, Leo and Joselyne appear to hold renewed hopes for the town's future.",
  str_mission_desc_4208110 = "Along the Illumina defensive line, Sharona leads the 1st Legion, trying to repel the Eclipsites. However, the sudden inundation of quagmire and attacks from fellow soldiers spark panic among the ranks...",
  str_mission_desc_4208111 = "Clean away the quagmires with the artillery reinforcement!",
  str_mission_desc_4208120 = "As Forsakin leads the quagmires in an assault upon the Illumina defensive line, an unsettling chorus of rattling wheels and galloping hooves echoes forth from the direction of Twilight...",
  str_mission_desc_4208130 = "The fierce battle rages on, with disoriented Illumina soldiers launching non-stop attacks against your side...",
  str_mission_desc_4208140 = "As Illumina's commanders analyze the current situation, Forsakin, upon receiving the Eclipse's signal of retreat, resolves to deliver a final blow to the Illumina soldiers...",
  str_mission_desc_4001010_long = [[
You stuck to activating the Colossus, even though you have tried over 17 years in vain.
Vice, an Aurorian girl, suddenly appeared in the Colossus when you were trying again.
Vice promised that she would get you out of here once you defeated the Eclipsites with your psychic ability.
Could you finally walk out of the Colossus?]],
  str_mission_desc_4001020_long = "You defeated the Eclipsites with your ability again.\nYou and Vice's team were friends now—\nCouldn't believe that you had friends even before visiting the world out there.",
  str_mission_desc_4001030_long = [[
Since the communicator was damaged, you were outnumbered by the Eclipsites without support.
Maybe everyone would be saved if you activated the Starlight Chamber.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001045_long = [[
You lost consciousness due to overusing your psychic ability to control the Colossus.
Another Aurorian, Ms. Blanc, joined you as reinforcement.
However, the signal markers have attracted a host of Eclipsites.
You had no choice but to start moving and find a way out.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001050_long = [[
You found Charon's target object, Zoya, an engineer, at the base station in no time.
Other than Zoya, a young man was still missing.
You couldn't turn a blind eye to it, so you crossed a group of Eclipsites to search for him.
Luckily, he was still alive!
Just that, you found that he was wounded, and that "he" was actually a girl.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001060_long = [[
Finally, you entered Undercity 28.
Charon got you and outsiders in, though he was quite stern.
After you defeated the escaped ones, you docked Soroz at the port.
Despite the limited resources in the undercity, the Colossus was getting replenished and was slowly recovering.
With the god-given break, you felt relieved and...passed out.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001070_long = [[
The Aurorians and you defeated the huge high-level Eclipsite Kraken together.
It was hardly the time to celebrate because a strong army of the Eclipsites was waiting for you.
For safe evacuation, to visit the new world...
Vice decided to try re-activating the Colossus with you.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001095_long = "You and Vice controlled the Colossus together. As the engine started... Soroz, shrouded in Aurora, has truly awakened.",
  str_mission_desc_4001080_long = [[
The warm-up was required for Soroz that was unused for 17 years.
However, you were exposed before the Eclipsites defenseless.
Defending the Colossus is top priority!]],
  str_mission_desc_4001090_long = [[
The impossible rescue operation was too difficult.
Never leave and never give up. Could you do it?
The far-off explosive sound discomforted Vice and you.
What happened at Charon's side?]],
  str_mission_desc_4001100_long = [[
The abnormality was getting closer from where Charon was responsible for.
Rush on to your destination and get ready for fighting against any formidable opponents!
Charon and Dayna were both right as a trivet. You were all reunited!
There was a ray of hope in a desperate plight:
Soroz was docked at the port nearby.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001110_long = [[
Soroz, as a hope in adversity, 
was going to help you escape.
No one knew whether there would be greater challenges.
There was no time to burden yourself with unpredictable difficulties. Shield the wounded and your companions to help them embark on the Colossus now.
Juts trim the sails!]],
  str_mission_desc_4001120_long = [[
You were badly injured by Eclipsites' fierce attacks.
Some of your companions fell in battle, while the rest put up a desperate fight to live.
Awaiting you was an uphill battle.]],
  str_mission_desc_4001130_long = [[
Soroz took off in everyone's anticipation.
However, another high-level Eclipsite, Nozard, appeared on the Colossus.
Bombarded with battles, everyone was too exhausted to fight.
Some of your companions sacrificed their lives to enable the rest to survive...]],
  str_mission_desc_4002015_long = [[
Since all of you were out of the danger for now, Vice convinced you to get back to Illumina with her first.
As you hesitated, Soroz, which was left unused over 17 years, was forced to land due to malfunction.
On the other hand, Nozard survived and didn't give up hunting you down...]],
  str_mission_desc_4002010_long = [[
The loud noise of the falling Colossus attracted countless Eclipsites. 
A new battle was coming.]],
  str_mission_desc_4002035_long = [[
Vice was badly hurt for protecting you from the Eclipsites when you were arguing with her.
At the critical juncture, a group of robbers claiming to be Sinsa defeated the Eclipsites.
You were saved but they claimed that the Colossus was then theirs.]],
  str_mission_desc_4002020_long = [[
Another battle was coming. But you had to count on the unidentified Rediesel Wrench guys.
It was great to know that these bandits could fight as well as the Aurorians!]],
  str_mission_desc_4002030_long = [[
Another battle was coming. But you had to count on the unidentified Rediesel Wrench guys.
It was great to know that these bandits could fight as well as the Aurorians!]],
  str_mission_desc_4002040_long = [[
Did Sinsa do it in a moment of weakness or have an axe to grind?
You had no say in this matter but to see what would happen next.
He led you to the base of Rediesel Wrench.
This street, Tail Street, was full of despairs and corruption.
Why did he bring you here?]],
  str_mission_desc_4002050_long = [[
The world was hierarchical and there were always dark corners you never knew about.
The fact was that you and Vice had a new understanding of the Rediesel Wrench...
You figured out at least one of Sinsa's purposes: 
They wanted to purge nonstarters with the help of Soroz.]],
  str_mission_desc_4002060_long = [[
The battle got off the ground, but everyone wondered why the Eclipsites could fight purposefully and organically.
The presence of Umbrahulk proved that they were right!
Just as Illumina's reinforcements arrived, the Rediesel Wrench guys left tactfully. 
Once again, your fate was decided by someone else.]],
  str_mission_desc_4002095_long = "You returned to Undercity 28 with Charon. Vice and Soroz were settled well.\nThe defense was impenetrable, but Charon and Hiiro still suspected that the Eclipsites had grasped the way to cross it.\nA few days later, Vice recovered. The short rest was interrupted by a new crisis —\nThe undercity started to shake and the alarm was triggered. What happened?!",
  str_mission_desc_4002070_long = "The Eclipsites pierced the defense at the out-of-sight corner of the undercity, and everything was in jeopardy.\nThe best way to protect the wounded and the citizens was to retreat. You could only launch a contingency plan.\nSome mystery underlay this affair, but you had no time to think it over—",
  str_mission_desc_4002080_long = [[
Sinsa and Eve once lived in an undercity before.
Eve was also reduced to "such look" there.
What was the truth?
What could history tell us?
Now, you could only continue to follow Sinsa's footsteps and complete his two requests...]],
  str_mission_desc_4002090_long = [[
You were swamped by waves of attacks from the Eclipsites.
If it went on like this, everyone would be in great danger!
Having faced similar trouble, you came up with an idea: the last hope was the Colossus.]],
  str_mission_desc_4002100_long = [[
The Eclipsites had gathered around the Colossus. You'd better retreat and destroy all the undercity's info as soon as possible.
But now, it was not the time to press the Red Key!]],
  str_mission_desc_4002110_long = [[
Everyone was on the Colossus, except Charon.
You couldn't leave Charon there like this, but you were nearly done up in battles.
Cruel abandonment was inevitable no matter what choice you would make...]],
  str_mission_desc_4002120_long = [[
The Red Key was pressed. Retreat now!
You defeated Nozard who rose again once and for all when breaking through the siege and fleeing.
Undercity 28 went up in smoke. As you were mourning for Charon...
A high-flown train charged out of the fire; it was Charon?!]],
  str_mission_desc_4003015_long = [[
Before reinforcements arrived, you sensed a call for help from a young man. Was he one of your people?
You attempted to seize the slim chance to find out the truth although it was a dangerous decision!
Vice decided to stand by you this time. The Caelestite would no longer need to fight alone.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003010_long = [[
A newly built stele stood on the cliff as the sun shone as usual.
Neither you nor Sinsa broke free from the sentiment of yearning.
New changes surprised you. Illumina's troops broke the stillness.
Vice and you returned to the team after settling the unexpected Eclipsites attack.
The Rediesel Wrench guys left, disappearing into the wilderness...]],
  str_mission_desc_4003020_long = [[
Mendelson, who protected the Think Tank Module, was attacked by Schummer.
Despite his best efforts to resist, his tattered and torn body could not change his fate.
Without the soldiers, he was forced to retreat and could only call for your help while being on the run.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003030_long = [[
"Time is running out," the mysterious young man called for help.
The Colossus excavations at ES-0096-F7 Relics came to a standstill unexpectedly. Hiiro also went missing.
You and Vice forcefully activated the Colossus to search for your superior.
Not only to prove your ability to commandeer the Colossus 
but also more so to save your companions.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003031_long = "TBC",
  str_mission_desc_4003040_long = [[
Members of the excavation team were assimilated into the Eclipsites!
You had to pull yourself together to fight your former companions.
Meanwhile, the Aurorian firewall of relics was corroded by dark power.
The Great Aviduz announced with her mighty power that she would purge betrayals and seek revenge for Mother.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003050_long = [[
You couldn't save the last survivor. Darkening was doomed to end like this.
Flower rain might save his soul...
Sakura cleansed his body and planted the Aurorian faith into his consciousness.
He told you an important message, that "they" are still here.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003060_long = "You finally found Mendelson who is badly wounded.\nHe was captured by his own soldiers because of Schummer's strong power.\nBattle imminent—",
  str_mission_desc_4003070_long = [[
A performance appeared to be over secretly somewhere else.
However, Schummer wanted to push the performance to another climax, to inject infinite Darkflow into the Colossus' core.
Vice perceived something, though it was foggy around.
You would just have to play it by ear. Intuitively, you could find a way to the end of the performance.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003080_long = [[
You were in fear but dying with dignity trumped living in disgrace.
The Caelestite was exterminated. So above all is to defend the future of everyone else!
Schummer got his hands on the Think Tank Module. Now it's only time before...
You had to move on to finish all this!]],
  str_mission_desc_4003090_long = "The figure in your mind was now standing in front of you, looking strange but familiar.\nThe frail young man was ECHO of the relic Colossus, Mendelson.\nMeanwhile, Hiiro and Zoya were buried in the rubbles of ruins.\nThe dying roar of Colossus echoed loudly in the ruins—\nThey had to hasten their pace in case of a second collapse.",
  str_mission_desc_4003091_long = "TBC",
  str_mission_desc_4003100_long = [[
Most systems went offline due to the damage done by Schummer.
It was hard to locate Hiiro and Zoya. They had to escape on their wits.
You and Vice went to complete 
a more important mission with Mendelson.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003110_long = [[
You were at where the Think Tank Module was stored, and Schummer...
might be waiting for you here.
Stop her! Affected by the dark energy, Mendelson's body became weaker and weaker.
Perhaps... this would be his last fight.]],
  str_mission_desc_4003120_long = "Schummer had left, and Tabaad waited for you there.\nThanks to Hiiro's assistance, Tabaad's body faded away in the sakura.\nEmbracing the last vision, Mendelson's life came to an end, leaving you clues:\nThink Tank Module, Autonomous Growth Unit, and Flame Control Module—these will be what Schummer comes after next...",
  str_mission_desc_4003145_long = [[
Right now, in the Lumopolis Archive, the Think Tank Module is locked up somewhere in a corner.
The prying eyes are closing in, which might indicate that the Eclipsites will attack Lumopolis soon.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004015_long = [[
A huge city in the sky heaved in sight. It seemed that your target, another Think Tank Module, was there.
Your old enemy, Schummer, had noticed Lumopolis. Things were looking blue.
Your priority was to convince the Guardians Captain, Carleen.
Suddenly, your conversation was interrupted by a surprise attack...]],
  str_mission_desc_4004010_long = "According to the townsfolk in Lower Lumopolis, they were assaulted by the Eclipsites, almost always at the east area. The Guardians went to investigate into it. But you chose to check the west area because of Carleen's instinct. The planted agent in the city whispered secretly: We'll have the freedom we're promised once we get our hands on that thing.",
  str_mission_desc_4004020_long = [[
The Eclipsites were spotted in the west area! The runaway ones raised the devil everywhere.
According to Gertzurde, a squadron leader of Lower Lumopolis, citizens outside the city needed to be escorted.
It seemed that he was once a famous knight as well...]],
  str_mission_desc_4004030_long = [[
The coordinates provided by Soroz pointed to Lumopolis Gardens which was heavily guarded in Lumopolis.
When Darkover arrived, 
the Great Aviduz lurking in the dark would move to grab Lumopolis Core.
Before the storm, you realized something big was coming up...]],
  str_mission_desc_4004040_long = [[
The Darkover turned Lumo Guards into Eclipsites.
Such a thing shouldn't be here. Lower Lumopolis was in danger!
You were blocked by the Lumo Soldiers when hunting down Shire to Lumopolis Gardens.
It was all about the Core and destiny of Lumopolis, so 
Vice did her best to convince Carleen, the captain of Lumopolis Guardians, to support your mission.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004050_long = [[
A new sighting from the west area! It seemed to be high-level Eclipsites this time!
Track and kill them all.
Carleen looked uneasy again.
No matter what, you got to move on.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004060_long = [[
Shelt teamed up with her sister to fight, but the scales were still tipping in your direction.
Smog concealed the Eclipsite sisters who were hightailing to 
a Lumo Noble's residence in Uptown!
Warning! Every Guardian, get back to defense now!]],
  str_mission_desc_4004085_long = [[
In Lumopolis Archive, Gertzurde is decoding the encrypted Think Tank Module.
Shelt told him that she would lure enemies to Uptown to buy him time.
Carleen realized that it would be a suicidal venture if they escaped to Uptown;
So she asked Raphael to search in the opposite direction while she tracked down the Eclipsite sisters.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004100_long = [[
Meanwhile, Raphael didn't find the suspicious man.
Instead, she met Gertzurde, the squadron captain, who just completed his mission.
He held a box covered with cloth. What did it contain?...]],
  str_mission_desc_4004110_long = [[
Following the blood trail, you came to a place near Uptown. The Eclipsite sisters had no way back.
They despairingly turned for aid to the mystery man only to be told that
they could only choose between defeating enemies and surviving.]],
  str_mission_desc_4004120_long = [[
"I'll turn into a dandelion... and fly away..."
The mystery man's lies and power transformed the sisters into freaky monsters.
Such power was a strong tool but an inhumane torture instrument.
The long-suffering sisters were finally reduced to ashes. The annoying crisis was resolved.
Gertzurde's mission was accomplished. So far, Schummer got the complete Think Tank Module...]],
  str_mission_desc_4005015_long = [[
Illumina Legion Commanders could not desert their post, and thus could not provide you with more help.
You had to track Schummer and find the Autonomous Growth Unit by your own.
Philyshy, the Intel Chief, brought a clue...
Meanwhile, Carleen applied for special order from Lumopolis;
she would chase after Schummer with you.]],
  str_mission_desc_4005010_long = [[
The number of fallen Colossi indicated the number of sacrificed Caelestites.
Now, you were finally at the Colossus relic of the Nameless 13, but you found you were in ruins.
Illumina's Director of Research, Gronru, was conducting some research here.
It was true that the Autonomous Growth Unit fell on the Colossus!
You needed Caelestite's power if you wanted to peel it off from the Colossus.]],
  str_mission_desc_4005020_long = [[
The interior of the fallen Colossus was badly damaged, so the path leading to the Autonomous Growth Unit was bumpy and turbulent.
The unusual shake heralded Schummer's arrival.
She unleashed her power without restraint and made fun of those ignoble and weak losers.]],
  str_mission_desc_4005060_long = [[
Minds of the dead were a poem as well as a song, intertwining in the void and conveying across space and time.
The second module was the last gift they gave you. Now, the Colossus started glowing again from its dormancy.
However, Schummer came from above.
To protect the modules you've got, Gronru summoned the throne to cover your retreat.]],
  str_mission_desc_4005070_long = [[
The terminal buzzed. 
It was a message from Gronru, ordering all of you to retreat quickly, but Schummer cut into her talking.
"Get back to the abandoned Colossus within 30 minutes and hand me the modules, or consider Gronru dead."
Toe the mark or save Gronru?]],
  str_mission_desc_4005090_long = [[
Just 5 minutes left before the deadline.
Soroz neither left nor landed. You had come to a decision.
Meanwhile, Gronru didn't just await her doom. She was stronger than one could imagine.]],
  str_mission_desc_4005120_long = [[
Even for Caelestites, grasping the Eclipsites' power actually allowed one to become so powerful?
Schummer won this as easy as pie. But beyond our expectation, she kept the boring promise. But she said as well, that sparing your life was mercy and compassion. Awaiting you the next time round was a deathmatch.]],
  str_mission_desc_4006015_long = [[
You had to find the Flame Control Module without a moment's delay even if you didn't get much support from Illumina and Lumopolis;
you decided to head to the distant Whispering Corridor yourselves.
The Whispering Corridor was like an intricate maze, and just as you were fretting, Shadowlord, the Ruler of Umbraton, sends you a competent companion,
Ms. Sheol, who would guide you in exploring this maze...]],
  str_mission_desc_4006010_long = "Your hunting operation went well even though you were only supported by Ms. Sheol remotely.\nArmy bootprints stood out from the Eclipsites' footprints—\nIt was Gertzurde, the traitor who was once a hero in Lumopolis.\nHe was led to believe the lie of Shelt's death, so hatred grew in his heart...",
  str_mission_desc_4006050_long = "You appeared to have found the right way to the Flame Control Module, but you couldn't let your guard down yet. Gertzurde seemed to be lurking ahead. Would this be your final battle with him?",
  str_mission_desc_4006060_long = [[
Gertzurde, who was determined to take revenge on you, was defeated although equipped with dark power.
He finally knew that the so-called truth was a lie that Schummer and the mystery man cooked up to control him.
Unfortunately, it was too late. Dandelions had gone with the wind...
Gertzurde was so grieved that he decided to bring you to where Schummer was.]],
  str_mission_desc_4006085_long = "A dozen years ago after the Darkover crisis was over, Gertzurde was knighted. He didn't feel happy in his marriage to a noble's daughter, so his fairytale beginning was without a happy ending, until he met Shelt, though it was a wrong choice.",
  str_mission_desc_4006070_long = [[
Eclipse knew of Gertzurde betrayal.
Guided by Gertzurde, the Flame Control Module was at your fingertips.
Waiting for you at that moment was your old friend, Nozard, who became powerful after being transformed by the mystery man.]],
  str_mission_desc_4006110_long = [[
You could sense that Schummer was lying in wait somewhere at the end.
You had known about the module identifier from Gertzurde, but this also means Schummer probably knew it as well!]],
  str_mission_desc_4006120_long = [[
Charon who sailed the Other End himself led Schummer to believe that it was Illumina's reinforcements.
Reluctant to risk it, the mystery man and Schummer left, leaving Gertzurde's body.
Carleen burned his body, then set off in the wind with Shelt...
Meanwhile, Lumopolis was facing an even greater crisis...]],
  str_mission_desc_4007015_long = [[
Schummer 's black Colossus arrived over the sky of Lumopolis.
Without shield protection, Lower Lumopolis was in great peril. Fortunately, a nearby Illumina Legion Commander came to its assistance.
Schummer would pay for what he did later, after this immediate threat was Schummer removed!]],
  str_mission_desc_4007010_long = [[
More and more Eclipsites gathered in Lower Lumopolis.
Given the lack of support from the soldiers, everyone could only take action separately.
However, you were again ushered into endless battles.]],
  str_mission_desc_4007050_long = [[
Thanks to your tactics, rescue and elimination operations in Lower Lumopolis were accomplished quickly.
Your connection with Soroz was very weak, but it seemed to be safe.
Just as everyone was relieved, Carleen learned that Uptown was under attack!]],
  str_mission_desc_4007060_long = "The black Colossus was a threat to the entire floating island,\nbut everyone managed to rush to Uptown in time and took Mara Sol down.\nThe battle ended in Schummer's arrogance. However, just then, you heard a call for help—\nWas the Colossus itself under attack?!",
  str_mission_desc_4007085_long = [[
You tried everything to connect with Soroz but failed.
Not wanting to guess the worst, the top priority was to get back to support Soroz right away.
Just when everyone was at their wits' end because there was no vehicle, 
Carleen flew a plundered airship to you like the savior she was.]],
  str_mission_desc_4007070_long = [[
Soroz was a mess after the Eclipsites invasion.
The worst consequence was foreseen, but you believed that Soroz was still alive.
Find Soroz before being spotted by Schummer!]],
  str_mission_desc_4007100_long = [[
You finally sensed Soroz after the hard-fought battle.
But it wasn't a call anymore, but instead a repeating message.
Did it mean... that Soroz had come to a bad end?]],
  str_mission_desc_4007110_long = "You haven't been able to sense Soroz since a while ago, \nand the throbbing pain in your heart is a reminder of the anomaly.\nAlas, Schummer said that Soroz was already—",
  str_mission_desc_4007120_long = [[
For Soroz, you battled it out with Schummer who was growing stronger!
The most surprising discovery was that another high-level Eclipsite, Forsakin, was one of the companions who previously belonged to Illumina!
Before you could be shocked, the black Colossus was charged.
Vivian planned to risk her life for your escape.
After a tremendous impact that brought incorporeality. What would you face next...?]],
  str_mission_desc_4008015_long = [[
A cry awakened you from a strange dream.
You were inside Aviduz with Vice, who never hesitated to come to your rescue.
You must now find a way to escape...]],
  str_mission_desc_4008020_long = [[
"No one shall be left behind."
With this in mind, you decided to rescue Chief Vivian first!
Meanwhile, the mysterious one continued to guide you...]],
  str_mission_desc_4008030_long = [[
As you moved onward, your body felt strange.
However, there was no time to check what's wrong, and you had to find Vivian as soon as possible.
Meanwhile, you were certain that Carleen must also be doing all she could to battle on...]],
  str_mission_desc_4008060_long = [[
The abnormality within your body couldn't be ignored. Something was definitely about to happen,
because when in battle, even the Eclipsites paid you no heed...
What was going on in the shadows?]],
  str_mission_desc_4008070_long = [[
As Curies barged her way through, you finally reached where Chief Vivian was being held,
and where Solfall, a powerful enemy, awaited you...
After defeating it, the mysterious one showed their true form and helped you get rid of a foreign matter known as the "seed."]],
  str_mission_desc_4008085_long = "In Lumopolis, Carleen failed to receive the support of the Lord.\nHowever, this didn't thwart her determination to use the ultimate weapon—\nIn at the control room, Carleen had decided to activate Damocles herself!",
  str_mission_desc_4008090_long = "Although Chief Vivian has been rescued, it wouldn't be wise to escape right now.\nThis was the turning point of the battle, and the group had become the key force to cripple the enemy from within.\nYou couldn't leave—you had to stop playing defense and attack instead!",
  str_mission_desc_4008100_long = "The battle was heating up, and Schummer was finally aware of your actions.\nIt seemed that this fierce battle was destined to take place in the core area of the Black Colossus—the bridge!\nMeanwhile, Damocles was also brewing the final storm...",
  str_mission_desc_4008130_long = "Standing before the long-coveted Lumopolis, what could Schummer be thinking right now?\nWould her mind be filled with the past, or perhaps with regret?\nYou should continue on—the source of all this laid ahead!",
  str_mission_desc_4008140_long = "The final battle at the bridge. The Eclipsites in your way were quickly disposed of.\nHaving no foreknowledge of Damocles, Schummer soon felt its destructive power—\nCarleen initiated the light cannon's attack, and with your help, she penetrated Aviduz.\nThe black gale finally fell in defeat...",
  str_mission_desc_4008155_long = "Meanwhile, as the battle died down—\nSeveral key figures set to steer the direction of the world revealed themselves from behind the scenes to take the center stage.\nAn overshadowing whirlpool of fate began to form. How would you navigate your ultimate destiny?",
  str_mission_desc_4009015_long = "After the Damocles Incident, a provisional punishment was handed down to Carleen, and the important task of finding out the cause of the incident fell to you.\nSchummer's \"body\" must be found, and this matter must be resolved if you wish to repair Soroz.\nAs chance would have it, Aviduz happened to crash in that familiar, yet strange place—Eraveil.",
  str_mission_desc_4009020_long = [[
The Eraveil awaiting you was very different from the one seen in your vision.
It was barren, lifeless, contaminated with a strange energy, and overrun with swarms of Eclipsites.]],
  str_mission_desc_4009030_long = [[
After the Colossus crashed in Eraveil, you were joined by members of the Rediesel Wrench on the way finding it.
Sinsa and Bopper were hoping to salvage some materials from the wreckage, but ended up becoming separated from their group.]],
  str_mission_desc_4009040_long = [[
You and Sinsa unexpectedly met again, but he didn't seem to know exactly where he had found himself.
However, this was no time to catch up. The first order of business was to start looking for Aviduz...]],
  str_mission_desc_4009050_long = [[
Although the exploration was going much more smoothly with Sinsa's help, the air was growing colder by the second.
The only explanation was that this place had now become a nest of Eclipsites...]],
  str_mission_desc_4009070_long = [[
You found a badge proving that one of the Eclipsites had once been an Aurorian.
It appeared that the mangled enemy before you had been in fact once just like your Aurorian companions.
You must end its pain.]],
  str_mission_desc_4009085_long = [[
Recovering from her grievous wounds within her healing pod, Schummer dreamt of herself long ago.
The Schummer of the past recounted her determination and desire fervently and awaited her rebirth.]],
  str_mission_desc_4009090_long = [[
You sensed sorrow and despair emanating from deeper within Eraveil.
Could this be an illusion or was it reality? Was Aviduz also crying out in agony?]],
  str_mission_desc_4009130_long = [[
Having defeated the Eclipsites in Eraveil, you were finally close to where Aviduz fell.
However, members of the clandestine True Order also seemed to have business here and were gathering something in the shadows...]],
  str_mission_desc_4009140_long = [[
Upon meeting once again, Forsakin seemed a little surprised that you hadn't "transformed" yet.
Before you had a chance to settle the score with her, she made her escape.
Before she did, however, she let slip a vital clue, finally confirming that Schummer was still alive.]],
  str_mission_desc_4010015_long = [[
Meanwhile, at the Lumopolis Medical Center...
Philyshy came to visit Vivian and informed her that you were chasing after Forsakin.
The two of them also briefly discussed the relationship between Forsakin and the Grand Marshal...]],
  str_mission_desc_4010020_long = [[
In order to continue your pursuit of Forsakin and find Schummer, you entered Aviduz.
Although Aviduz had crashed long ago, its wreckage still exuded a powerful degree of Darkflow.
What's even more disconcerting was the fact that the Eclipsites within it were all running away in a hurry, as though something terrible was awakening nearby...]],
  str_mission_desc_4010030_long = [[
Still recovering from her wounds, Schummer had awakened early and was feeding on Eclipsites in order to regenerate energy!
Although you couldn't make heads or tails of her decline into even deeper depravity, you must move on and find your undying foe!]],
  str_mission_desc_4010070_long = [[
Your enemy collapsed in death's arms once again.
Forsakin's cruel and immoral indifference pushed you past the point of vexation. You must find her and Schummer!
Meanwhile, in the course of your pursuit, more information surrounding Schummer's past came to light...]],
  str_mission_desc_4010085_long = "On that day seventeen years ago, Schummer became the harbinger of Eraveil's fall.\nShe issued the cry of chaos on behalf of the Eclipse. Some were forced to accept it, while others fought to the death in resistance.\nBut in the end, the Caelestites were doomed. She used their freshly-spilled blood to complete her long-sought goal—her dark evolution.",
  str_mission_desc_4010090_long = [[
After taking a glimpse of Schummer's past, you saw that your dream of Eraveil mirrored the tragedy of that distant memory.
The road of revenge had gone on long enough. It's time to find Schummer and put an end to it all.]],
  str_mission_desc_4010130_long = "Forsakin finally pushed Schummer past the point of no return, forcing her to undergo a massive breakthrough in power—\nHowever, she lost all control as a result. In a state of utter madness, she appeared before you once again.\nOnly one of you would come out of this battle alive.",
  str_mission_desc_4010140_long = "You defeated the crazed Schummer, but there seemed to be an endless flow of power within her.\nIn order to recover the Seed, Forsakin drained her of her power.\nSchummer, who lived solely for her own twisted crusade for justice and rebirth, finally died amidst a tide of Eclipsites—\nJust like her own people did, many years ago.",
  str_mission_desc_4010155_long = [[
With the help of the Rediesel Wrench, everyone managed to escape from Aviduz unscathed and left Eraveil.
You also managed to successfully connect the Think Tank Module obtained from Schummer with Soroz, and the repairs seemed promising so far.
Now, you couldn't help but wonder where your next adventure would take you...]],
  str_mission_desc_4101015_long = "Soroz became unstable without the Echo Template. If this lasted any longer, the damage might ensue. You and Vice decided to visit an Undercity located at the border of the land of Eternal Night following the lead provided by the Think Tank Module.",
  str_mission_desc_4101020_long = "Arriving at Undercity 80 at the border of the land of Eternal Night, you realized Eclipsites had claimed this place as theirs since Illumina's abandonment. The intense Darkflow made it almost impossible to use Luminatics. Under these circumstances, you start the investigation cautiously.",
  str_mission_desc_4101030_long = "You and Vice advanced deeper into the Undercity. Traces of war could be seen everywhere under a thick layer of dust accumulated over the long years. In the ruins, you discovered some discarded Colossus modules...",
  str_mission_desc_4101040_long = "The piece that could be used to repair Soroz's Echo Template was embedded in a machine in the core chamber. You struggled to take it off, which caused the energy core of this Undercity to stall. Without power, the Undercity began caving in and a High-Level Eclipsite emerged during the collapse.",
  str_mission_desc_4101055_long = "You and Vice engaged the High-Level Eclipsite with the extra burdens brought by the Darkflow while seeking for opportunity to escape. However, the Eclipsite completely cut your way. At this crucial moment, Reinhardt came to your rescue. To your surprise, that High-Level Eclipsite seemed to be an old comrade of hers.",
  str_mission_desc_4101060_long = "Reinhardt led you onto a different escape route toward the ground. But the Darkflow grew heavier as you ascended—it was already after nightfall. The battle would only become harder from there.",
  str_mission_desc_4101070_long = "Under your continuous questioning, Reinhardt began retelling a story from the past. Her comrades once fought an arduous battle with her in Undercity 80. She broke out of the enemy's encirclement to seek help but only to discover that Illumina had left them behind to save the majority of the population.",
  str_mission_desc_4101080_long = "You reached the ground level in the deepest dark right before dawn. Forsakin and the High-Level Eclipsite were waiting in silence. Reinhardt asked you for help. She wanted to give it one last try to bring her old comrade back.",
  str_mission_desc_4101090_long = "Forsakin aroused the High-Level Eclipsite's deeply buried hatred and changed its appearance. A deadly battle was imminent. Reinhardt sustained severe injuries to protect you. In this hopeless situation, she put up a brave resistance...",
  str_mission_desc_4101105_long = "Threatened by the Eclipsite army, Vice and you brought the badly wounded Reinhardt back to Soroz and headed for Illumina's lifeline. On the way, Reinhardt recalled something from the past. Some changes of great importance seemed to be brewing inside Illumina's solid Undercity...",
  str_mission_desc_4201015_long = "Following the clues you managed to obtain, you set off to Eraveil in search of the Colossus Maintenance Base in hopes of finding a way to return Soroz to its original state. However, things don't go exactly as planned...",
  str_mission_desc_4201020_long = "On the way to Eraveil, Soroz is attacked by Eclipsites in what appears to be a planned ambush. During the battle, Eclipsites' attack shatters the Colossus' control panel, and Soroz begins to fall...",
  str_mission_desc_4201040_long = "You crash-land in a vast space at the base of a white tower. According to Soroz's data, this is the \"Tarmac,\" so the base you're looking for should be nearby. Time to grab the metal detector and start exploring.",
  str_mission_desc_4201050_long = "As you start searching, some Eclipsites following you quietly surround the White Tower. In order to continue the search, you blow up the entrance to the Tarmac with Barton's help and prevent them from coming any further.",
  str_mission_desc_4201060_long = "Following the entrance you discovered, you enter a vast base beneath Eraveil, and you come across many traces of the Caelestites who had lived here before, which you never knew existed.",
  str_mission_desc_4201070_long = "After a fierce battle, you fell unconscious from the lack of oxygen. By pure chance, you connected with the AI that controls the base. With its help, the ventilation was turned on and you regained consciousness. Under the AI's guidance, you continue exploring the base...",
  str_mission_desc_4201090_long = "You arrive at a vast space in the base, and there are signs that this area was once known as the Exiled Zone, and that those exiled here in the past were Caelestites. Here, you find a Lance Rifle that once belonged to a Caelestite and successfully use it to defeat Eclipsites.",
  str_mission_desc_4201100_long = "Pursued by a powerful Eclipsite, you're left with no choice but to use the defensive devices of the underground base to deal with it. But these devices aren't only for attacking Eclipsites, they're dangerous to Aurorians as well. Vice is also injured and falls into a strange unconscious state known as \"hibernation.\"",
  str_mission_desc_4201115_long = "In order to find a cure for Vice and repair Soroz, you continue your exploration of the base's core. There, you come across a strange machine—Circular System—one that only you, a Caelestite, can use. From this machine, you get a glimpse of some unknown secrets.",
  str_mission_desc_4201120_long = "You manage to find a record of an Aurorian awakening from hibernation in the Circular System. But due to age, you're only able to access fragments of information. You decide to explore the depths to find more clues.",
  str_mission_desc_4201140_long = "As the base's system suddenly starts rebooting, you lose control of the base and become the target of its attack. The base's Guardians have awoken from a deep slumber, and you must defeat them to regain control of the base.",
  str_mission_desc_4201155_long = "As you regain control of the base, the reboot completes, giving you full access. Amidst rumbling tremors, the tower starts to rise, slowly revealing its original form. Creations of ancient technologies all over Astra begin to resonate strangely...",
  str_mission_desc_4202015_long = "Upon gaining administrative access to the Obelisk of Return, you learn about a device called \"Chord Link\" that can save Vice. However, as the Obelisk of Return has fallen into disrepair, there's no information about this device in the system, so you'll have to go to the area where it's located to investigate further.",
  str_mission_desc_4202020_long = "As you search for the Chord Link, Barton follows Forsakin's trail into the tower. However, he's gotten lost in the vast Obelisk of Return...",
  str_mission_desc_4202040_long = "In the wake of Barton's pursuit, Forsakin abandons her plan to follow you and resorts to force. You have to play for time to crack the Access Control of the Chord Zone under Forsakin's attack.",
  str_mission_desc_4202050_long = "You flee to the Chord Zone to avoid Forsakin, but the act of cracking the Access Control triggers the Chord Zone's defenses. With all the traps in the passageway activated, you're faced with a challenging obstacle. Just when things come to a head, you trigger a trap explosion, briefly stopping Forsakin and entering the Chord Zone.",
  str_mission_desc_4202060_long = "In order to protect Vice and defeat Forsakin, Barton, who's severely wounded, decides to transform himself with the Chord Link. During this time, Forsakin commands Eclipsites to break down the gate. To buy Barton time, you face off against Forsakin.",
  str_mission_desc_4202070_long = "As Barton completes the synchronization, he gains new powers and steps out from the Chord Link to join you in fighting Forsakin. As the tide turned, Forsakin flees in the chaos with Barton following closely behind...",
  str_mission_desc_4202085_long = "Barton's success assures you, and you put Vice into the Chord Link for synchronization. Through the Obelisk of Return's surveillance, you see Eclipsites assembling a large army outside the tower and Aurorians from all sides fighting hard. As you witness this, you make up your mind to drive these Eclipsites out of Eraveil with your own hands.",
  str_mission_desc_4202090_long = "Since it'll be a while before Vice wakes up, you and Carleen are faced with no choice but to leave her in the Chord Link in order to chase Forsakin out of the tower. At this time, the scene outside the tower is one of horror, with overwhelming numbers of Eclipsites and Aurorians battling hard. It's as if time has gone back to the day when Eraveil was attacked seventeen years ago...",
  str_mission_desc_4202100_long = "Under Eclipsites' relentless attacks, everyone is steadfast, doing their best to hold out. Then, the Eclipse reveals their trump card—Darkflow cannons. These unexpected weapons immediately place you at a disadvantage. The hope of victory seems to be fading quickly...",
  str_mission_desc_4202115_long = "As everyone outside the Obelisk of Return remains locked in battle, in order to turn the tide, Reinhardt suggests leaving some behind as a diversion while she and you ambush the Eclipsites. To protect Eraveil, you decide to team up with Reinhardt.",
  str_mission_desc_4202130_long = "With Reinhardt and Forsakin locked in battle, the tide has yet to turn. Sensing an imminent crisis, you decide to head back to the Obelisk of Return and seize access to the Core Ring to activate the Obelisk of Return's ultimate weapon—the Chord of the Law.",
  str_mission_desc_4202140_long = "In order to gain access to the Core Ring, you face the Guardians alone, but you're unable to defeat them. Just when you're about to be defeated, Vice, who has just recovered from hibernation, arrives at your side with her new powers. You two work hand in hand to defeat the Guardians and finally activate the Chord of the Law.",
  str_mission_desc_4202155_long = "The \"gift\" Master Francis left for you allows you to successfully activate the Chord of the Law, keeping all Eclipsites away from the Obelisk of Return and bringing the battle to an end. Unable to activate again due to the lack of energy, the Obelisk of Return becomes a monument to history, and everyone wonders what will happen to it...",
  str_mission_desc_4203015_long = "Vice's body suddenly started emitting a strange light, a possible side-effect of using the Chord Link. Worried about the situation, you contact Vivian in hopes that she can identify the source of the problem.",
  str_mission_desc_4203020_long = "Out of concern for Vice's safety, you agree to help a team of researchers from Illumina investigates Soroz's new functions. During the investigation, the researchers discover a massive amount of ancient combat data; they now wish for you to access this data using Illumina's Battle Simulator and conduct further research on it.",
  str_mission_desc_4203030_long = "You conduct a number of tests using the Battle Simulator, a sophisticated device used to create near-perfect combat scenarios. After seeing the simulator in action, Reinhardt believes that by producing even more complex battles, this device can even be used for training purposes.",
  str_mission_desc_4203040_long = "You enter the Battle Simulator once again, but the environment within has been changed into a Dark Zone. Within this dark and hostile simulation, your goal is to defeat the Eclipsites and break through their encirclement.",
  str_mission_desc_4203050_long = "Using the terrain to eke out a small advantage, you finally defeat the last of the simulated Eclipsites. Battered and bruised, you and your allies emerge from the Battle Simulator after a hard-fought victory and find Reinhardt speaking to the other researchers. You overhear part of their conversation and discover that Reinhardt personally lived through the battle you just experienced...",
  str_mission_desc_4203060_long = "You return to the simulator, and the environment has been drastically altered once more. The Aurorians in the simulation use weapons you have never seen before and are desperately fending off wave after wave of bloodthirsty Eclipsites. As they fall to the monsters one by one, the virtual world seems to grow more and more hopeless...",
  str_mission_desc_4203070_long = "Inside the simulated battle, the tragedies of an apocalyptic war assault all your senses. Desperate soldiers, rampaging Eclipsites, and a demonic monster the likes of which you have never seen surround you... Suddenly, an error occurs in the simulator, and just when you are about to fall to Jormungand's vicious attack, Soroz inserts its consciousness into the battle and manages to pull you out. When you regain your senses, you are shocked to realize...",
  str_mission_desc_4203085_long = "The Science Council, an organization that holds the Illumina Federation's most well-kept secrets, has personally invited you and Reinhardt to meet with them. Whatever their motives are, they are the most capable of understanding Soroz's condition right now. As you enter the conference room, a looming sense of unease overtakes you. Suddenly, Reinhardt gently places her hand on your shoulder, breaking the oppressive tension hanging over the room.",
  str_mission_desc_4203090_long = "By the end of the meeting, you and Algol come to an agreement of sorts. At his request, you initiate a Mind Link with Guardian One, an ancient machine in the Illumina Federation's possession. Doing so will benefit both parties: the Illumina researchers will have a chance to observe a Caelestite's interactions with an ancient device, and you will have a chance to ask Guardian One for its help.",
  str_mission_desc_4203100_long = "In the process of establishing a Mind Link with Guardian One, you realize that despite existing for countless years, this artificial intelligence has the personality of a mere child; as such, it will only trust those who interact with it with honesty and fairness. After sensing your concern for Soroz, Guardian One immediately resolves to help you rescue Soroz's consciousness.",
  str_mission_desc_4203110_long = "Guardian One leads you to the simulated battlefield in which Soroz is located. The aftermath of an ancient catastrophe from eons past lies before you, one in which Eclipsites still roam the lifeless planet. Knowing that the simulation is nearing its end, you must search for your cherished companion amongst the ruins of a dying world before it all comes crashing down.",
  str_mission_desc_4203120_long = "In the wreckage of a shattered world, you finally find Soroz and access its database. Familiar with the things around you, yet unsure of the time or place in which they exist, your stupor is finally broken when Guardian One tells you that it has discovered a number of ancient records inside the terminal. Here, the Caelestites are far from home, wandering in an aimless direction...",
  str_mission_desc_4203130_long = "Guardian One tells you that in order to repair Soroz, you must first enter its memories and troubleshoot the errors in its data. With Guardian One's help, it should be a simple enough task. While entering Soroz's memories, you see more and more of the terminal's records. In them, the Caelestite's appear to be growing fewer in numbers...",
  str_mission_desc_4203140_long = "With Guardian One's help, you successfully clear out the errors in Soroz's database. With your mind still on the terminal records, you decide to access them once again. Inside the records, you witness a miracle: under the care of the Caelestites, the Colossi are born and given sentience. After this brief miracle comes a long wait, a stretch of time so long and uneventful that it requires every ounce of your focus to reach the end. Suddenly, a familiar scene unfolds before you: Eraveil.",
  str_mission_desc_4203155_long = "After exiting the virtual world, you return to the conference room once more. The Science Council has begun discussing the events they just witnessed. They believe that Soroz is operational once more, but have concluded that the Colossus' sentience was nothing more than the result of an accident. To truly restore Soroz's consciousness, you must travel to an even more distant place...",
  str_mission_desc_4204015_long = "Entrusted with the Science Council's Fragile Combat Cyborg, your next assignment is to make contact with the Illumina troops stationed in the town of Twilight. There, you must exchange the droid for the resources necessary for restoring Soroz's consciousness. You have never heard of this town, which is situated on the Illumina front lines; much to your surprise, you find Carleen there on an outside assignment.",
  str_mission_desc_4204020_long = "The town of Twilight, located near the Aurora Ruins and bordering the Eternal Night zone, is a melting pot of different military factions. The Lumo Knights stationed here have already made contact with Carleen; it seems Beretta and Yingel have two very different understandings of this remote and isolated place. As the Eclipsites begin their assault, the fragile object in your hand begins to emit a strange sound...",
  str_mission_desc_4204030_long = "A strange sound awakens you from your dream, and Soroz is nearly \"removed\" by Sean. As it turns out, Sean rushed over from Twilight after receiving a message about your arrival some time ago. His plan was to welcome you while also carrying out his usual \"removal\" work, which includes clearing Eclipsites from the area around Twilight, as well as any other suspicious invaders. For a grassroots officer like Sean, this is just common practice.",
  str_mission_desc_4204040_long = "When Axelia, Yingel, and Sean greet one another, you realize that the three of them have a common history. They explain that they are \"graduates\" from the Phospherus Program, a program spearheaded by the Science Council for the purpose of nurturing children into super soldiers. Although the three of them have grown much since then, they still tease and laugh with one another like they did as children.",
  str_mission_desc_4204050_long = "Despite the savage conflict surrounding Twilight, its residents are more concerned with taking shelter from an imminent natural disaster. The aurora overhead threatens to surge out of control, and everyone is desperately seeking shelter to weather the impending energy storm. The Eclipsites take advantage of the widespread panic and begin attacking indiscriminately. Just as you decide to enter the fray and save the townsfolk, you discover that reinforcements have already arrived in the form of a regiment of Lumopolis soldiers: the Ironthorn Knights.",
  str_mission_desc_4204060_long = "In the face of seemingly insurmountable odds, the Ironthorn Knights easily break the ranks of the Eclipsites before bearing down on them. After seeing Leo's incredible combat prowess in action, you decide to help the knights fend off the remaining Eclipsites. Just as the tides seem to shift in your favor, however, a new and even more vicious threat emerges...",
  str_mission_desc_4204070_long = "A fresh wave of Eclipsites enters the battlefield, and the Lumo Knights are unable to fend off their attacks while also protecting the townsfolk. You break away from the front lines to defend them, but the Eclipsites are relentless in their assault. Just as you reach your limits, a young girl suddenly appears in the midst of the battle; with a blinding, holy light, she instantly dispels every Eclipsite in the immediate vicinity. With the townspeople safe, you rejoin the fight without hesitation and ultimately claim victory. Afterward, the mysterious girl known as Joselyne invites you to have dinner with her in Twilight",
  str_mission_desc_4204085_long = "Joselyne takes you to a restaurant in Twilight and tells you more about the town: its history, its troubles, and most importantly, its ties to a lost and ancient Colossus. After finishing your meal, you return to the Illumina Researcher, who helps you fully restore Soroz's consciousness, if only temporarily. In those brief moments, Soroz points you to a certain location: an Undercity deep within the Dark Zone, where the ancient Colossus lies dormant...",
  str_mission_desc_4204090_long = "You decide to journey to the location that Soroz mentioned and are given the support of both Illumina and Lumopolis, as well as the newly-acquainted Joselyne. After seeing their impressive might on the battlefield, the threat of the Eclipsites seems much less daunting than before.",
  str_mission_desc_4204115_long = "You and your allies proceed deeper into the ruins. Wary of the sheer number of Eclipsites roaming the area, your party proceeds with the utmost caution. At this time, however, Sean decides to challenge Axelia to a contest of strength: whoever defeats the most Eclipsites is the winner and the stronger of the two.",
  str_mission_desc_4204120_long = "You finally arrive on the Bridge of the Colossus, and begin your search for the necessary module. Upon finding it, however, you discover that the module has long since fused itself to the Colossus; removing it by force would only cause more damage. Axelia then steps in and provides you with a device that can copy the module's data, but says that it will take some time...",
  str_mission_desc_4204130_long = "After fending off the attacking Eclipsites, Axelia's device finally finishes copying the module's data. Just as your party decides to evacuate, the Colossus begins to rumble violently; is it about to go out of control? In order to pacify the Colossus and protect the settlements near the ruins, you decide to initiate a Mind Link with the Colossus...",
  str_mission_desc_4204140_long = "It appears that the rumbling was not caused by the Colossus... So what was responsible for it? After establishing a Mind Link with the Colossus, you discover that a large number of Eclipsites have gathered outside of it; within their ranks, you sense the presence of an extremely powerful entity...",
  str_mission_desc_4204155_long = "You return to Twilight with Axelia and the others in tow and say your farewells. With your precious data finally in hand, you journey back to Illumina. Only time will tell if this data will actually help to restore Soroz; all you can do is wait. It is at this moment that you receive an invitation from Illumina's top brass, a request to travel to a hidden Undercity where yet another Chord Link exists...",
  str_mission_desc_4205015_long = [[
Holding Vice hostage, Forsakin is forcing you to go with her, seemingly after a Chord Link secretly uncovered by Illumina, with the intention of completing experiment data through Vice.
On another front, the battle in Twilight has intensified as Leo sends distress signals to both Lumopolis and Illumina.]],
  str_mission_desc_4205020_long = "To complete the experiment, Forsakin coerces you into fighting the Illumina soldiers and delaying them. Just hope she keeps her promise of not killing anyone.",
  str_mission_desc_4205030_long = "You've arrived at the destination, where Forsakin, who's familiar with the surroundings, called the Institute X that she built! Before you can ponder further, she wants Vice to initiate the Chord Link! What is going to happen?",
  str_mission_desc_4205040_long = "Forsakin isn't pleased with the result of the Chord Link's operation. You and Vice try to ambush her, only for her to then summon a mob of Eclipsites to oppose you.",
  str_mission_desc_4205041_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4205050_long = [[
You're no match for Forsakin and fought to no avail. Helios appears next to Forsakin and isolates you from Vice, forcing you both to comply.
Meanwhile, Ulysses calls Yingel in for a secret meeting and tasks her with a special mission.]],
  str_mission_desc_4205065_long = [[
In the besieged Twilight, Leo receives not aid but an invitation to a Joint Military Exercise, which he takes as a chance to alert the world of the threat from the Dark Zone.
Meanwhile, Illumina and Lumopolis also begin preparing for the exercise, as if the mastermind behind it vowed to see it to the end...]],
  str_mission_desc_4205070_long = [[
After Forsakin separated you and Vice, you have no means of contacting her other than a communicator. You keep going as Forsakin starts digging into the archives for info on the Phospherus Program.
Meanwhile, Yingel meets up with Intelligence Officer Anatoli with a secret order, it seems her goal is Institute X as well.]],
  str_mission_desc_4205080_long = "To find the missing you and Vice, as well as uncover what's really behind the joint exercise, Carleen arrives in Illumina to speak to Gronru, who points her to Institute X, where she meets Yingel by chance and finds out about the crisis here.",
  str_mission_desc_4205090_long = "Forsakin tries to get more info on the Phospherus Program but accidentally triggers the defenses. After defeating them, she changes the keywords and successfully accesses the files.",
  str_mission_desc_4205100_long = "You lose contact with Vice when the communicator runs out of power, but not before giving Yingel and others time to figure out Vice's exact location.\nYet, when Yingel gets close, she realizes a powerful foe is guarding Vice—Helios.",
  str_mission_desc_4205101_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4205110_long = [[
Yingel and Helios are locked in a fierce struggle. She also realizes Forsakin will likely sense the battle.
Meanwhile, Carleen reaches you. She tries to defeat Forsakin and get you out of here, only to be mired in an uphill battle of her own.
The desperate sight of Helios teaming up with Forsakin prompts Yingel to boldly incinerate the Chord Link...]],
  str_mission_desc_4205120_long = "The so-called inferno turns out to be a mere illusion by Yingel, but it turns the tide of battle and gives your side the edge. Yingel also tries to convince Forsakin that Reinhardt never abandoned her after the lab fire and that her so-called revenge was misguided from the start.",
  str_mission_desc_4205130_long = [[
Refusing to give up, Forsakin cuts off the power to the lab and seals the door, buying herself and the Chord Link time to further upgrade Helios.
Meanwhile, Ulysses' motive is slowly coming to light, as he takes a very keen interest in the result of Forsakin's experiment...]],
  str_mission_desc_4205140_long = [[
Finally, Forsakin merges three different enhancements on Helios, drastically altering his appearance. After the battle ends, Helios surprisingly regains his senses, though with a somewhat fragmented memory.
Meanwhile, Wrath and Reinhardt arrive to confront Forsakin, but she still manages to get away.]],
  str_mission_desc_4205155_long = [[
No one can find Forsakin in Institute X and speculates she might be hiding near Gannon. Meanwhile, the Joint Military Exercise commences as planned in that city, as representatives from various powers convene and fight for the title of the best army.
But in Gannon's shadow, Forsakin and Helios lurk...]],
  str_mission_desc_4206015_long = [[
The exercise begins, drawing to Gannon teams from Lumopolis, Illumina and Twilight, as well as your trio and another mysterious squad.
Vivian informs you of the rules and indicates that the victor will be honored to challenge the Grand Marshal.
Meanwhile, in the corner of the city, Forsakin awaits fellow Eclipse members to rescue her and Helios.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206020_long = "First up is the familiar Battle Simulator for everyone to relive arduous campaigns from the past. Many suffer defeat against the overwhelming odds, except for Leo's squad from Twilight, which gains a miraculous victory.",
  str_mission_desc_4206030_long = "Next is the classroom portion, wherein one can exchange course credits based on grades and performance for supplies. Thus, under Wrath's tutelage, everyone delves into the fine art of \"brawling\"...",
  str_mission_desc_4206040_long = [[
A supposedly harmless training is sabotaged and almost ends in a disaster. Guess the competition between squads isn't so friendly, after all.
Meanwhile, given Leo and Yingel's outstanding performance, you decide to apply for extra simulator sessions, but someone rigs that, too...]],
  str_mission_desc_4206041_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4206050_long = [[
For the Eclipsites coming out of nowhere in Gannon, Leo and Zhao go above their authority to command Illumina soldiers to a resolution. Wrath isn't too keen after finding out, but comes to appreciate Leo's talent.
In a conversation, Wrath also learns the desperation in Twilight and realizes the higher-ups seem to be censoring the news...]],
  str_mission_desc_4206060_long = [[
Lessons move forward into actual combat in the Joint Military Exercise. Under your advice, everyone defeats all adversaries through a temporary alliance, bringing the event to the final segment: Capture the Flag.
Everybody begins spending course credits earned on gear and props in anticipation of the big battle to capture the flag in the Undercity.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206070_long = "Going into the Undercity in search of the flag, you, Carleen, and Vice are strategizing when that mysterious squad from Umbraton runs up with a band of Eclipsites in tow...",
  str_mission_desc_4206080_long = [[
You finally put an end to the Eclipsites following a chaotic battle, but the Umbraton squad that started the trouble refuses to enter the Undercity with you, as if they got their own mission.
Meanwhile, the two strongest squads, Team Leo and Team Yingel, start fighting each other somewhere.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206090_long = "With the mysterious squad seemingly manipulating your route, you run into a dangerous spider monster.\nFollowing a tough battle, you rush to where the flag is only to find the fight between Team Leo and Team Yingel over, with the winner being—Team Yingel.",
  str_mission_desc_4206105_long = [[
Team Leo is very content with being the runner-up since they did it as a favor in exchange for Illumina sending reinforcements to Twilight.
Meanwhile, Ulysses furthers the plan to attain his goal through Forsakin's actions in Gannon.
Indeed, on-site to fight the Grand Marshal, Yingel receives news of an Eclipsite invasion in the city. You, Leo, and others decide to help her in the matter.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206110_long = [[
In the showdown against the Grand Marshal, Axelia displays an unusual level of power and a death wish. Reinhardt also senses something odd in the exhibition match.
Meanwhile, Eclipsites' diversion clears Forsakin and Helios to escape Gannon through a secret passage.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206120_long = [[
The Eclipsites in Gannon seem to be drawing your attention on purpose, but you cannot just break off and let them run amok either. In the meantime, you also sense the presence of Figerald the Wraith.
In the arena, Axelia's near-suicidal offense is starting to concern Reinhardt.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206121_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4206130_long = [[
Reinhardt concedes just to stop Axelia from her own suicidal attacks, but that also falls right into Ulysses' plan.
You, Leo, Yingel and others hurry to the Wraith's location, where Guardian One's mainframe is kept!
Meanwhile, Forsakin and Helios get to the rendezvous spot only to discover Esien has already sent soldiers there. They realize the Eclipse has set them up.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206140_long = [[
Relegated to a mere sacrificial pawn by the Eclipse, Figerald is thoroughly defeated and detained. But another unknown Wraith has taken Guardian One's core and there's nothing anyone can do about it.
As for Forsakin, she gets away clean when Helios stays behind to cover the escape.
Back at the arena, Ulysses reveals that the Committee has found evidence of Reinhardt harboring Forsakin in her residence, placing the Grand Marshal under arrest in front of everyone.]],
  str_mission_desc_4206155_long = [[
And this is where things stand. Even if you find Reinhardt being removed from duty a hard pill to swallow, it's still a fact.
As for Ulysses, he is very content with intercepting Forsakin's experiment results, but the Wraith capitalizing on the opportunity to steal Guardian One does mar the operation.
What is going to happen to Reinhardt? And what unknown enemies lie in the shadow?]],
  str_mission_desc_4207015_long = "The Illumina Federation is underway with its third public trial of Reinhardt on charges of treason. As you and Vice wait outside the interrogation chamber, word eventually reaches you that Reinhardt has been stripped of her Grand Marshal title and sentenced to imprisonment. The news leaves you both wondering about the possibility of a monumental upheaval on the horizon.",
  str_mission_desc_4207020_long = "As you find yourselves puzzled by the current situation, Vivian, rushing over in haste, calls Vice aside, speaking of an immediate mission in her grasp. You arrive at the Illumina Station and discover that accompanying Vice on this mission is not only Charon but also three contestants who claim to come from Umbraton. Upon hearing this, a sense of unease washes over your heart.",
  str_mission_desc_4207030_long = "As you're lost in thought about who could guide Illumina's path forward, the broadcast suddenly announces Wrath's appointment as the new Grand Marshal. Amidst your astonishment, Leo rushes over to inform you about the encroachment of Eclipsites upon Twilight. He implores you to pilot the Colossus and accompany him to provide aid. Meanwhile, within a certain laboratory in Illumina, a secret plan is silently underway.",
  str_mission_desc_4207031_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4207040_long = "Amidst the watchful gazes of onlookers, the freshly appointed Grand Marshal, Wrath, leads the new military forces to assemble at the station, alongside the cutting-edge war machine, Engine VII. Even though Wrath now stands in the position she's longed for, she's well aware that she hasn't yet triumphed over Reinhardt fair and square. Thinking about that, memories of her past challenges against Reinhardt begin to surge within Wrath's heart.",
  str_mission_desc_4207050_long = "With a clear understanding of her own strength, Wrath had long anticipated the results of the Grand Marshal's final selection. Despite finally stepping into Reinhardt's shoes, it's not the path she had hoped for. Hence, Wrath makes an inner resolve to temporarily hold the position of Grand Marshal until Reinhardt's return, committing herself to outperforming her role in every way possible.",
  str_mission_desc_4207060_long = "Fueled by Joselyne's motivation and encouragement, the soldiers valiantly stand their ground against the Eclipsites' onslaught. Meanwhile, you and Leo finally reach the entrance of Twilight. Although Leo is reluctant for you to join this dire battle, your advantageous role as a Caelestite and the Colossus' pilot convinces him otherwise. In the end, it's your reinforcement that reignites the soldiers' morale on the battlefield.",
  str_mission_desc_4207075_long = "Planning to request support from Lumopolis, Zhao inadvertently becomes the captive of Istvan's underlings. In the Royal Court of Lumopolis, Schwartz holds several pleas for assistance in his grasp, while the nobles debate whether to dispatch reinforcements. In the end, Schwartz commands the supporting troops to maintain their position at the Lumo Stronghold, refraining from involvement in Illumina's military operations.",
  str_mission_desc_4207080_long = "With the Eclipsites' attack escalating in intensity, even the experienced Leo finds himself stretched thin. Just as the group debates between a daring assault or continued retreat, Wrath leads the Illumina Guard Legion onto the battlefield, turning the tides of the battle in Twilight.",
  str_mission_desc_4207090_long = "Forsakin becomes aware of the \"Seeds\" implanted within these soldiers, designed to enhance their combat capabilities. Despite her discontentment over Ulysses for pilfering her experimental findings, she realizes that the formidable Eclipsites brought forth by Wraith are in favor of her subsequent actions. Meanwhile, you sense the surge of tremendous Darkflow yet still are oblivious that the nightmare in Twilight has only just begun.",
  str_mission_desc_4207100_long = "Upon investigating the abnormalities among the Illumina soldiers, Leo and Wrath have a heated discussion about issues within the ranks of her forces. In hopes of uncovering the cause of the soldiers' anomalies, Wrath seeks your assistance. While you delve into the consciousness of a corrupted soldier and find a boundless mire within, in the real world, Twilight is also suffering the relentless incursion of mud and Eclipsites.",
  str_mission_desc_4207110_long = "Witnessing the soldiers' grim fate as they're chewed down by the Eclipsites during the experiment, Yingel finally realizes the true purpose of the \"Phospherus Program\": They're implanting \"Seeds\" within Aurorians and selecting exceptional soldiers via combat against Eclipsites! Just as Yingel attempts to halt the experiment, an out-of-control subject suddenly launches a violent assault against them.",
  str_mission_desc_4207111_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4207120_long = "After a thorough investigation of the battlefield alongside Wrath, you gradually unravel why the Illumina soldiers are prone to the mud's influence. Meanwhile, the mud relentlessly extends its reach into Twilight, as the enemy acting as the command center seizes the opportunity to launch an assault. With Wrath charging ahead, you take command on the battlefield but accidentally get caught by the mud.",
  str_mission_desc_4207130_long = "As you watch Wrath recklessly charge into the midst of the Eclipsites, you decide to employ a Force Boost to enter her consciousness and rouse her from within. From a suppressed council chamber to the rain-soaked Gannon City, and the sight of Reinhardt lying on an operating table... At last, amidst the ever-shifting scenes of Wrath's consciousness, you manage to locate her presence.",
  str_mission_desc_4207140_long = "You and Wrath finally locate the last squad of Illumina forces. Encouraged by Wrath's words, Axelia gradually regains her mobility. After your extensive search, the main enemy reveals itself, while Leo arrives, leading the Expedition Knights. Nevertheless, to protect her team from the mud's corrupting influence, Wrath decides to confront the enemy on her own.",
  str_mission_desc_4207155_long = "Just a few days ago, Wrath received a notice from the Committee—succeed Reinhardt as the new Grand Marshal of Illumina, on the condition of participating in the \"Phospherus Program.\" With her aspiration almost within reach, Wrath realized her ambitions were undergoing a quiet transformation. In the end, she agreed to the Committee's terms, yet a plan also formed secretly within her heart.",
  str_mission_desc_4208015_long = "Beyond the borders of Twilight, changes are also taking place. As the Illumina Recon Team tracks the core of \"Guardian One,\" they stumble upon unexpected and crucial leads. Meanwhile, within the Royal Court of Lumopolis, Hydrad, serving as Istvan's envoy, discusses with Schwartz matters of reinforcement. At long last, Schwartz reaches a decision—to protect the Aurorians the Lumopolis way.",
  str_mission_desc_4208020_long = "Under the mud's influence, some Illumina soldiers mutate into Eclipsites, launching assaults against their own comrades. Confronted with this dire scenario, Leo organizes the evacuation of Wrath's subordinates even as he handles the turned soldiers personally. Amidst the chaos, injured Wrath returns to the fray, trying to bring back those ensnared in a rabid frenzy.",
  str_mission_desc_4208030_long = "Given the limited medical resources in Twilight, you decide to divide into three teams for the rescue operation. Wrath continues the search for the missing Illumina soldiers, while Joselyne escorts critically wounded soldiers to seek refuge in Lumo Stronghold. As for you, Leo initially suggests that you pilot Colossus and take the refugees to safety in the Eraveil, but you stand your ground, insisting on staying to weather the storm with everyone.",
  str_mission_desc_4208040_long = "Charon appears to have anticipated Victoria's arrival, yet is taken aback when knowing the bizarre resistance encountered isn't Victoria's doing. Vice, upon learning of the situation in Twilight, grows concerned for your safety and, aided by Victoria, journeys to the town. However, after a brief stay, the strange force strikes Charon's train once again.",
  str_mission_desc_4208041_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4208050_long = "The revelation from the Bloody Bible leaves everyone baffled. Victoria then swiftly realizes that the Wraith's \"Domain\" has enshrouded the train. To escape from the \"Domain,\" Charon fights the Wraith head-on, while Victoria and three of her subordinates perform a sacrificial rite to break free from the predicament. Right at the moment when Vice breaks through the encirclement, your psychic ability catches the rhythm of Vice's heartbeat.",
  str_mission_desc_4208060_long = "You intend to save this soldier with your psychic ability. However, even though witnessing the soldier's pre-battle experiences, you still can't halt his descent into madness. At the very moment, the soldiers are starting to go into rabid one after another. As Leo suggests that he'll go and put them down, Wrath, taking a stand as the Grand Marshal, chooses to personally grant a merciful end to those comrades tormented beyond measure.",
  str_mission_desc_4208070_long = "As the city gate swings open, an otherworldly beam of light prompts everyone to bow in reverence. Devout Joselyne recognizes this as the divine radiance brought forth by the \"Saintess\" of Lumopolis Temple. The \"Saintess\" tends to the wounded, acknowledging Joselyne's efforts, and resolves to journey with her to Twilight to help those still in need.",
  str_mission_desc_4208080_long = "Forsakin chuckles, saying these fallen soldiers are her \"work of art\" meticulously crafted for all to behold. Wrath's rage blazes, yet she doesn't act recklessly, wary of the \"Seed's\" influence over her body. In her way to reclaim the soldiers Forsakin has taken away, Axelia bears witness to the gruesome spectacle of soldiers turning on each other. In the direst moment, a reinforcement team arrives.",
  str_mission_desc_4208095_long = "Vivian recognizes Anatoli as the source of the signal and recalls how he had obstructed her during a mission at Illumina Prison. It turns out Anatoli employed this very method to test Vivian's resolve, and he ultimately decides to aid her in completing her plan. Just as the two believe the plan is progressing smoothly, the signal is abruptly cut off.",
  str_mission_desc_4208100_long = "The battle in Twilight solidifies Leo's determination to stand as the town's guardian. Joselyne, deeply aware of the conflicts between factions, expresses to the \"Saintess\" her resolution to establish a shelter for the Aurorians within the church. However, the war is far from over. Upon learning that multiple forces have converged on Illumina's defenses, you all decide to regroup and advance toward the defense line.",
  str_mission_desc_4208110_long = "Amidst the soldiers' intense battle, Barton and Hiiro arrive as reinforcements. After sharing the current situation, Sharona remains anxious about Wrath's safety. However, Reinhardt's timely appearance bolsters everyone's confidence. As it turns out, Wrath's plan involves not only defending Twilight but also rescuing Reinhardt and regrouping with them at the frontline.",
  str_mission_desc_4208111_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4208120_long = "Wrath intends to lead her troops and encircle the Eclipsite army, but \"Engine VII,\" under the influence of Darkflow, becomes an unexpected hurdle. Just when Axelia is in a tight spot battling \"Engine VII,\" Reinhardt comes to the rescue. With a mixture of satisfaction and relief, Reinhardt watches Wrath rejoin the frontline, yet Wrath steps aside willingly, giving Reinhardt the reins to command the unfolding battle.",
  str_mission_desc_4208130_long = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4208140_long = "Before making her exit, Forsakin, manipulating both the Illumina soldiers and Engine VII, launches a final, brutal attack against the Illumina military. Reinhardt perceives Forsakin's involvement in the Eclipse's operation and tries to reason with her, urging her to comply with her own will. However, Forsakin's response drives a growing wedge between the once-sisters. Soon after, Lumopolis and Twilight soldiers join the battle in the defense line.",
  str_mission_desc_4208155_long = "Rain falls upon the Illumina frontline. As it stops, the mud dissipates, revealing the earth under the sunlight once again. Wrath gazes upon the heavy casualties, blaming herself for her failure as Grand Marshal. However, Reinhardt commends her performance, asserting that it was her unwavering determination that protected Twilight and its soldiers. However, the real battle still looms ahead.",
  str_mission_limit_4000001 = "Navigator, go fight and clear the stage with <color=#e8d9bb>Vice</color>!",
  str_mission_limit_4000002 = "Deploy your squad members and fight with <color=#e8d9bb>Vice</color> together!",
  str_mission_limit_4000003 = "You'd better deploy other teammates to clear the stage with <color=#e8d9bb>Vice</color>. Try it out!",
  str_mission_leader_limit_4000002 = "Navigator, <color=#e8d9bb>Vice</color> is the best Captain candidate!",
  str_mission_desc_4209015 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4209020 = "A vivid nightmare startles you awake several days later in the wee hours...",
  str_mission_desc_4209030 = "In your excitement, you take off without getting a time or location for the rendezvous, and things certainly don't look good in Illumina right now...",
  str_mission_desc_4209040 = "You are shocked by how Algol makes her debut but even more surprised by her parasitic \"pet\".",
  str_mission_desc_4209050 = "You and Vivian are in awe when Algol brings you to her office. There is actually a place like this in Illumina?",
  str_mission_desc_4209065 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4209070 = "Several Eclipsites suddenly appear in the Illumina Tech Park and block your path...",
  str_mission_desc_4209080 = "The Eclipsites keep pouring out of the building, but what shocks you more is that Ulysses is quietly following behind them...",
  str_mission_desc_4209081 = "It seems that these Illumina Soldiers undergo a fearsome transformation at night. Be careful!",
  str_mission_desc_4209090 = "Ulysses' words are laced with threats, and you have seen danger in his visions...",
  str_mission_desc_4209100 = "During the fifth review conference, Ulysses reminisces about a chapter from his past...",
  str_mission_desc_4209115 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4209120 = "What does that long-sealed prototype have to do with Ulysses?",
  str_mission_desc_4209121 = "These Eclipsites have greatly enhanced counterattack capabilities, so try not to engage them in melee combat.",
  str_mission_desc_4209130 = "In his excitement of reading the Engineer's notes, Ulysses strayed further and further away from his own research...",
  str_mission_desc_4209140 = "Through Ulysses' computer, you have discovered that he accessed an unrecorded warehouse without authorization...",
  str_mission_desc_4209150 = "After defeating the super-soldiers, you turn your attention to the still-running prototype...",
  str_mission_desc_4210015 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4210020 = "Ulysses insists his experiments benefit Illumina and strives to prove his point, but that severely displeases Anatoli, who's just nearby...",
  str_mission_desc_4210030 = "To expedite the decryption, you have mind-linked with Bool to find clues.",
  str_mission_desc_4210045 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4210050 = "Just when Algol thinks you have collected enough information, an X-factor shows up...",
  str_mission_desc_4210060 = "What will happen when you log into the Guardian's system?",
  str_mission_desc_4210070 = "When a crisis breaks, some people panic, and some simply can't wait...",
  str_mission_desc_4210071 = "The place where the Illumina Soldiers are performing their secret mission seems to be Lumopolis...",
  str_mission_desc_4210080 = "Ulysses arrives at Warehouse Zero and eagerly opens the present he has been readying for years...",
  str_mission_desc_4210090 = "At that sound, you suddenly realize the meaning of those vivid yet surreal dreams...",
  str_mission_desc_4210100 = "You rush out without a thought, only to find yourself having lost the perception of it...",
  str_mission_desc_4210110 = "The foe's taunting has riled you up. What response will you make as a Caelestite?",
  str_mission_desc_4210120 = "The Engineer has shown signs of backing down, but Gannon's defense core is still missing. What to do now?",
  str_mission_desc_4210121 = "The powerful super soldiers can enhance all your enemies, so you must stop them!",
  str_mission_desc_4210130 = "After the core gets replaced, you hear Ulysses speaking in a totally foreign tongue...",
  str_mission_desc_4210140 = "Before his vision collapses, he recalls a war-time conversation in the sanitarium...",
  str_mission_desc_4210155 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4209015_long = "After a violent tremor, you and the soldiers of Twilight return to Eraveil after a long absence. The Twilight survivors prepare a bountiful feast; after eating your fill of a perfect meal, you start a conversation with Soroz.",
  str_mission_desc_4209020_long = "Worried about Vice's safety, you sit on your Colossus terminal for days on end, waiting anxiously for any word from Reinhardt. Suddenly, you finally receive that long-awaited message.",
  str_mission_desc_4209030_long = "As the result of a problem with Illumina's defense system, you are attacked by Eclipsites in Illumina's service yard. Just then, the person who invited you here appears in a most unexpected way.",
  str_mission_desc_4209040_long = "Algol introduces her companion Bool, and explains her reasons for inviting you to Illumina. She suggests that Soroz's data files may contain clues regarding Guardian One's Core, which will hopefully lead to discovering Vice's whereabouts.",
  str_mission_desc_4209050_long = "As you drink a cup of coffee prepared by Guardian One, Vivian seems to finally relax somewhat. After a brief respite, everyone gets to work. Unfortunately, no one told you about Bool's unique and rather painful method of communication...",
  str_mission_desc_4209065_long = "After a lengthy analysis, you discover a flashing set of coordinates hidden within Soroz's data files, which appear to predate Eraveil by quite some time. Algol suspects that the birthplace of the Colossi lies deep within the Dark Zone, so you approach one of Illumina's expert physicists to ask about the coordinates.",
  str_mission_desc_4209070_long = "After defeating the Eclipsites, you discover that their bodies bear a startling resemblance to that of Aurorians. Barton, who was patrolling the Illumina Tech Park, joins your group and everyone surmises that these Eclipsites were most likely escaped test subjects from Ulysses' laboratory. With Alglol's help, you head for the laboratory and prepare to question the researcher.",
  str_mission_desc_4209080_long = "Ulysses does not deny that the Eclipsites from before had escaped from his lab, and he invites you deeper into the building for what he calls a \"small experiment.\" Curious about a number of things he mentioned, you accept his invitation.",
  str_mission_desc_4209090_long = "After witnessing a dangerous and horrific scene, Ulysses is taken away by Illumina Federation authorities. While you are still unsure as to why he showed you these things, it seems as though the sun is starting to shine on Gannon City once again. You and your friends hope that this crisis will end soon.",
  str_mission_desc_4209100_long = "Years ago, a younger Ulysses devoted himself to improving Aurorian survivability. While researching Illumina's genetic engineering technology, which had been passed down from centuries ago, he discovers a name long forgotten by history. Seeing this name fills him with hope for the future of all Aurorians.",
  str_mission_desc_4209115_long = "Joyce tells you about a floating stone, which had appeared at the coordinates within the Dark Zone, and the information matches the images you saw in Ulysses' mind. Only then does Algol realize that Ulysses has been hiding his work on the Guardian prototype all along.",
  str_mission_desc_4209120_long = "At the hearing, everyone is shocked to learn that Ulysses has been secretly researching on the ancient machine. As these revelations unfold, you and Algol continue searching Gannon City for the prototype. Just as dangerous as this machine, however, are the Darkflow-emitting super-soldiers hiding in the shadows.",
  str_mission_desc_4209130_long = "Ulysses proposes a bold experiment, which causes Robby, his long-time colleague, to suspect him. Who is \"the Engineer,\" and how did he convince Ulysses to take such radical measures with his research?",
  str_mission_desc_4209140_long = "When Algol arrives at Warehouse Zero, she is excited to discover that the Guardian prototype is still operational. Unfortunately, your intrusion also triggers an attack by the super-soldiers being stored in the building.",
  str_mission_desc_4209150_long = "When Algol first saw the prototype, she was still a student of Ulysses. More surprising, however, is the fact that Ulysses kept it operational in his private warehouse even after it was sealed away for safety reasons. As you and your friends attempt to access the mysterious prototype, you are filled with a mixture of anticipation and dread.",
  str_mission_desc_4210015_long = "You are taken aback by Bool's impressive functions and processing speed. As Algol recounts the tale of how they first met, you slowly realize the meaning behind the labels on her body.",
  str_mission_desc_4210020_long = "It comes to light that Undercity 80's true purpose was to screen candidates for the Artificial Sun project. While gathering crucial information about the project, Anatoli's recon team is ultimately wiped out. Unwilling to accept the loss of his team, Anatoli demands that the Committee try and punish Ulysses for his crimes.",
  str_mission_desc_4210030_long = "After using your psychic powers on Bool, you are overwhelmed by an endless surge of numbers and sequences. To extract the information you need, Algol shares her trick for handling difficult workloads with you. You try again, and apparently manage to obtain some useful data.",
  str_mission_desc_4210045_long = "Just like Yingel and Axelia, Sean is also a product of the Phospherus Program. However, Sean was deemed a failure at the start of the program, and sent away to Twilight. After learning about his origins, Sean begins to wonder if his purpose in life is to become a merciless weapon of war.",
  str_mission_desc_4210050_long = "Linking with Bool's mind causes you no small amount of dizziness and discomfort. Algol gives you a limit of two minutes, during which time you are instructed to retrieve as much information as possible. Thankfully, you emerge relatively unscathed, but something seems to be troubling Algol. What in the world could have brought down a civilization advanced enough to create this technology?",
  str_mission_desc_4210060_long = "You are caught off-guard by the situation in Gannon City. Algol continues desperately searching for a way into the system, only to discover that the violent tremors are being caused by an unseen enemy. Ulysses' trial is also temporarily suspended. Just when you think the crisis is almost over, the unseen enemy appears on the prototype's screen...",
  str_mission_desc_4210070_long = "Ulysses claims to have already devised a way to defeat the enemy, and Belisaria agrees to his operation, changes the previous preparations, and urgently launches the pre-made plan.",
  str_mission_desc_4210080_long = "The super-soldiers stored in the warehouse are the result of Ulysses' years of scientific research, as well as his gift to the Engineer. However, much to Ulysses' surprise, the Engineer soon takes control of them and uses them to attack all Illumina compatriots.",
  str_mission_desc_4210090_long = "\"Go home, Caelestite.\" A cryptic message for many, but one that you have heard in your dreams countless times. Who is he? Where exactly does he want you to go? As you struggle at your wit's end, you suddenly receive news that Soroz has been activated.",
  str_mission_desc_4210100_long = "The moment of farewell has finally come, yet you feel nothing. For reasons unknown, you have played this scenario out in your mind more times than you can count. Danger follows closely in the wake of your sorrow, but a tiny friend steps in and blocks a fatal blow meant for you.",
  str_mission_desc_4210110_long = "Within Figerald's consciousness, you appear to witness the process by which the Engineer enslaves others. Not only that, you see distant memories of a yawning abyss and skeletal remains of Colossi emerging from within Figerald's mind...",
  str_mission_desc_4210120_long = "To protect Gannon City, Algol's companion, Guardian One, resolutely offers up its own Core. Meanwhile, in order to obtain enough computing power for the transition, Reinhardt enacts an emergency protocol to redirect the processing power of every computer in Gannon City to their location.",
  str_mission_desc_4210130_long = "Algol discovers that the computer language used by the Guardian System is somehow related to the language used by the Eclipsites. Ulysses boasts that he can change the entire world, but you have no desire to live in a world modified by his hands.",
  str_mission_desc_4210140_long = "Which is more tragic, the loss of faith or the inability to realize one's dreams? Ulysses asks you one final question before falling at your feet. No longer able to reply, this may be the last time he ponders this question.",
  str_mission_desc_4210155_long = "After lying unconscious for three days, you awaken to discover that the crisis in Gannon City has already passed. However, what awaits you now is an even more dangerous exploration mission. You recall how you were saved while using your powers, and wonder if anyone in that shining, lake-like space can offer you the guidance that you seek.",
  str_mission_desc_4301015 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4301020 = "Within a vast temporary command center, the Committee of Joint Astra Expedition convenes a pivotal conference concerning the future of the Aurorians.",
  str_mission_desc_4301030 = "Due to encountering extreme air currents, your aircraft unexpectedly plummets onto the snowy plains at the edge of Northland...",
  str_mission_desc_4301040 = "You track the blood trail, yet it mysteriously vanishes along the way...",
  str_mission_desc_4301055 = "As Bethlehem escorts you out of the cave, she senses the unique energy field within and devises a solution to overcome the predicament.",
  str_mission_desc_4301060 = "Facing the current crisis in Northland, Bethlehem seeks counsel from the Snow Fox Elder on awakening the Primal Haven to cleanse the pollution plaguing the snow plains.",
  str_mission_desc_4301070 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4301080 = "As heavy snow blankets the border, you reach the tribe that nurtured Tiare, starting to search for the third pine tree.",
  str_mission_desc_4301090 = "With the awakening of the Primal Haven, a new beacon is erected. Tiare brandishes her powerful spear, charging once more toward that mighty Eclipsite.",
  str_mission_desc_4301105 = "—",
  str_mission_desc_4301015_long = "Bethlehem reminisces about a past encounter. Years ago, while patrolling the Snowpine Forest at the edge of Northland, she had a brief encounter with the Snow Fox living there. Tiare, the child raised by that Snow Fox, now serves as Bethlehem's guard, living in the Winter Palace, yet still worries about her tribe.",
  str_mission_desc_4301020_long = "Delegates from Lumopolis, Umbraton, and the Courier Union have exchanged opinions on the exploration preparations of the Illumina Federation. After the meeting, Reinhardt assigns you and Carleen to investigate the establishment status of the Northland outpost.",
  str_mission_desc_4301030_long = "Accidentally stumbling into the territory of the border tribe, you're perplexed by the bloodstains strewn across the ground. Subsequent reactions from Tiare and the Snow Foxes suggest that matters are not as simple as they seem. Despite their vehement opposition, you still decide to follow them to see what exactly happened.",
  str_mission_desc_4301040_long = "Overcoming your inner fears, you employ your Psychic Abilities to track down Tiare and the snow foxes. Eventually, you stumble upon the bloodstains they left and unexpectedly learn that two of your Rediesel Wrench friends have also come to Northland with your aircraft. But little did you know, a powerful Eclipsite is lurking nearby.",
  str_mission_desc_4301055_long = "Led by the Snow Fox Elder, you arrive at the ancient altar guarded by the Snow Fox tribe for generations. Here, your strength resonates with the ancient power, and the legend of the \"Three Pine Trees\" unfolds. To the Snow Fox Elder's surprise, it wasn't the royal family who took the pines, but rather the pines chose the royal family and acknowledged the queen.",
  str_mission_desc_4301060_long = "As Bethlehem faces the Eclipsite alone, you decide to search for two other pine trees together with Tiare. Novio suggests that since the ancient power has waned, to find the pines, you must seek clues from the legend of the \"Three Pine Trees.\"",
  str_mission_desc_4301070_long = "Carrying you on her shoulders, Tiare dashes all the way, eventually arriving at the Northland Court. When you're at a loss, Zarya's words offer a clue. It turns out that the pine tree chopped down has long been crafted into the queen's throne, but since the queen never sits on it, the throne has been gathering dust in the court.",
  str_mission_desc_4301080_long = "Delving into Tiare's memories, you uncover the disagreement between the Snow Fox Elder and Tiare's grandmother regarding her future. The key issue of their dispute is something about a stone slab symbolizing an ancient commitment, which is precisely what you're seeking. With the help of Tiny One and Roy, you manage to locate the third pine tree and bring it back to the altar.",
  str_mission_desc_4301090_long = "Tiare's attack sparks memories in the Eclipsite, reminding him of his past and the reasons behind his relentless training. As he attempts a final strike against you, you force him out of Northland. Under the Beacon's light, you take a historic step forward, venturing into the Dark Zone.",
  str_mission_desc_4301105_long = "Despite the Eclipsite remaining undefeated and the Northland outpost still under construction, you resolve to make active preparations and press on with your exploration into the Dark Zone in the coming time. Before leaving, you receive the Lumina Ore delivered by Tiare. Standing nearby, Bethlehem finds solace and contentment, knowing that the Northland guard, Tiare, has grown up and matured.",
  str_mission_desc_4220020 = "You find Pepita, but she puts on a grand escape act. She has been wanted by various factions, but why?",
  str_mission_desc_4220030 = "Pepita's friend is a Wraith, and they look like a pair of lunatics...",
  str_mission_desc_4220040 = "Pepita and Ursura meet, both haunted by their pasts.",
  str_mission_desc_4220050 = "To protect Pepita, who operates in the Dark Zone, Reinhardt makes a pact with Schwartz. But will the Heretics Investigation Division really accept that?",
  str_mission_desc_4220060 = "The region known as \"Coral Grounds\" is eerily beautiful, yet it reeks of death.",
  str_mission_desc_4220061 = "These Eclipsites seem familiar, but there's something deeply strange about them.",
  str_mission_desc_4220070 = "A mysterious race once thrived here until the Wraiths...",
  str_mission_desc_4220071 = "The eternal night is their home, and they are trapped in its endless cycle.",
  str_mission_desc_4220090 = "Faced with Ursura's restraint, Pepita burns herself to declare her defiance—No!",
  str_mission_desc_4220100 = "The Heretics Investigation Division finally faces the biggest \"heretic\" just as they wished. But Victoria's confidence in showing up alone speaks volumes.",
  str_mission_desc_4220110 = "As the eternal night draws near, Victoria unleashes her arcane power—when the \"sun\" rises, how will Ursura fight back?",
  str_mission_desc_4220015_long = "As your aircraft soars through the night, tracking the expedition team and Vice, a mysterious ball of light has caught your attention. Meanwhile, Reinhardt and the Committee are taking action. A new \"shadow\" is now in the spotlight.",
  str_mission_desc_4220020_long = "You come across Pepita's team in the Dark Zone, but she flees the moment she sees you. Philyshy's intel reveals that Pepita is wanted by both Illumina and Lumopolis. Soon after, the Lumopolis team shows up. They've dealt with her before, but the Committee swooped in before they could arrest her last time.",
  str_mission_desc_4220030_long = "Pepita shows up and fools everyone. Not only is she unaffected by the Dark Zone, but she's now on the side of the Wraith and has a powerful familiar from them. After stirring things up, she casually walks off with the Wraith, arm in arm.",
  str_mission_desc_4220040_long = "Pepita recalls her childhood, when her father betrayed her and lived a life controlled by the Committee. They replaced her frail heart with a strong artificial one, leaving her no choice but to follow their orders. Despite everything, she still doesn't want to hurt others.",
  str_mission_desc_4220050_long = "Pepita's condition runs in the family, but after her father sold her out to the Committee, she stopped trusting Illumina and ended up rebelling and joining the True Order. While Reinhardt and Schwartz want to get her back on the right track, the Captain of the Heretics Investigation Division isn't so sure about that.",
  str_mission_desc_4220060_long = "Guided by the Captain of the Heretics Investigation Division's treasure, you find yourselves in an unknown area. It appears that Aurorians once lived here, but they've been gone for a long time.",
  str_mission_desc_4220070_long = "You touch the corpse and glimpse the past of the Tundra Tribe. These people were trapped by Ursura's coral, spending their entire lives working for a certain furnace with no freedom. Every now and then, Yodu, a Wraith, would check their progress. But one day, Yodu decided they were no longer worth it and slaughtered everyone.",
  str_mission_desc_4220085_long = "Pepita, stuck with a heart controlled by the Committee, looks at Ursura's coral heart with envy. Ursura makes her an offer: if Pepita agrees to be hers forever, she'll make a coral heart for her. Recalling their first encounter, Pepita decides she'll never submit to anyone.",
  str_mission_desc_4220090_long = "Pepita sticks to her \"be free or be dead\" principle and cuts ties with Ursura.\nYou find a barrier that blocks Darkflow, but suddenly, Victoria shows up, claiming it as hers. As things start heating up, Ursura shows up chasing Pepita—but oddly enough, she gets scared off the second she sees Victoria.",
  str_mission_desc_4220100_long = "The expedition team couldn't agree on whether to attack Victoria, causing the group to break apart. The Captain of the Heretics Investigation Division charges at Victoria alone and gets defeated. Victoria then reveals a truth—now you finally realize that the light guiding you all along was Vice, who had fallen into the depths of the Pristine River.",
  str_mission_desc_4220110_long = [[
Victoria goes after Ursura alone and takes her on in a fight. Under Victoria's secret technique, Ursura is easily defeated.
Meanwhile, Charon runs into a "dead relative" named Wilhelm. To save Vice, Charon swallows his pride and starts learning the vampire's secret technique from him.]],
  str_mission_desc_4220125_long = [[
Pepita runs back to the base but is hunted by the Captain of the Heretics Investigation Division and the Committee's Executioner...
Deep in the eternal night, Figerald is somehow reassembled by Eclipse members, only to be used as stepping stones for Forsakin to become a Wraith.
With Ursura's resurrection, the new Eclipse members gather together, discussing Victoria's secret technique...
After falling off the cliff, Pepita is saved by her familiar, making her realize Ursura is still alive. Charon's train also breaks through space and locates her...]],
